PVD("serbia_vision_2021-2030",{"docs":["","RS Agenda 2030 report 2021"],"s":{"1":[[1,"12","32","Public Financial Management Reform Programme","Public Financial Management Reform Programme for the period from 2021 to 2025",""],[1,"22","2","Public Financial Management Reform Programme","Public Financial Management Reform Programme for the period from 2021 to 2025 with its accompanying AP should enable the realization of a sustainable budget through better financial management and control, strengthening the internal audit process and linking budget planning with public policies of the Government.",""],[1,"35","3","Fiscal Framework for Basic Services","The general government fiscal framework, which is an integral part of the Fiscal Strategy for 2022 with projections for 2023 and 2024, determines expenditures for basic services (education, health and social protection).",""],[1,"47","6","Medium-Term Fiscal Consolidation Framework","The Fiscal Strategy envisages a gradual balancing and stabilization of public finances in order to reduce the share of public debt in GDP and create the basis for stable economic growth.",""],[1,"82","2","Public Financial Management Reform Programme","The key strategic document is the Public Financial Management Reform Programme for the period from 2021 to 2025, with its accompanying Action Plan.",""],[1,"87","8","Public Finance Management Reform","The programmes adopted in the period from 2020 to 2021 additionally contributed to the attainment of the goals within the Fundamentals: Public Finance Management Reform, e-Government Development and Tax Administration Transforma- tion.",""],[1,"116","8","Public Finance Management Reform Programme","Public Finance Management Reform Programme for the peri- od 2021 to 2025 with its accompa- nying AP for the period from 2021 to 2025",""],[1,"118","9","Public Finance Management Reform Programme","Public Finance Management Reform Programme for the period 2021 to 2025 with its accompanying AP for the period from 2021 to 2025",""],[1,"119","7","Public Finance Management Reform Programme","Public Finance Management Reform Programme for the period 2021 to 2025 with its accompanying AP for the period from 2021 to 2025",""],[1,"120","7","Public Finance Management Reform Programme","Public Finance Management Reform Programme for the period 2021 to 2025 with its accompanying AP for the period from 2021 to 2025",""]],"2":[[1,"12","37","Tax Administration Transformation Programme","Tax Administration Transformation Programme for the period from 2021 to 2025",""],[1,"82","3","Tax Administration Transformation Programme","Responding to the problem of inefficient tax service, the Tax Administration Transformation Programme for the period from 2021 to 2025 (no accompanying AP) was adopted.",""],[1,"87","8","Tax Administration Transformation","The programmes adopted in the period from 2020 to 2021 additionally contributed to the attainment of the goals within the Fundamentals: Public Finance Management Reform, e-Government Development and Tax Administration Transforma- tion.",""],[1,"118","8","Tax and Revenue Collection Capacity Mobilization","Mobilise resources and capac- ities for tax and other revenue collection (17.1)",""],[1,"118","9","Tax Administration Transformation Programme","Tax Administration Transforma- tion Programme for the period from 2021 to 2025 (no AP)",""]],"3":[[1,"12","4","Programme for Improving Management of By-Products of Animal Origin","Programme for Improving Management of By- Products of Animal Origin for the period from 2020 to 2024",""],[1,"76","2","Animal By-Products Collection System Development Programme","2020 to 2024, with the accompanying AP for the period from 2020 to 2024, focuses on providing a basis for starting the development of the system of collecting animal by-products (SPŽP), as well as facilities that meet the requirements in terms of construction and level of equipment.",""],[1,"76","3","Strategy for Improving Facilities for Dealing with Food of Animal Origin","Strategy for Improving Facilities for Dealing with Food of Animal Origin for the Period from 2016 to 2020 with the accompanying AP, contributes to the attainment of targets 2.3 dou- ble the agricultural productivity and incomes of small-scale food producers and 2.4. ensure sustainable food production systems.",""],[1,"89","3","Programme for Improving Management of By-Products of Animal Origin","Programme for Improving Management of By-Products of Animal Origin and Strategy for Improving Facilities for Dealing with Food of Animal Origin contribute to increasing the level of food safety and preserving human and animal health.",""],[1,"89","3","Food of Animal Origin Safety Strategy","Programme for Improving Management of By-Products of Animal Origin and Strategy for Improving Facilities for Dealing with Food of Animal Origin contribute to increasing the level of food safety and preserving human and animal health.",""],[1,"95","7","Food of Animal Origin Facilities Improvement Strategy","Strategy for Improving Facilities for Dealing with Food of Animal Origin for the Period from 2016 to 2020, with the accompanying AP for the period from 2016 to 2021",""],[1,"95","7","Animal By-Products Management Improvement Programme","Programme for Improving Management of By-Products of Animal Origin for the Period from 2020 to 2024, with the accompanying AP for the period from 2020 to 2024",""]],"4":[[1,"7","3","Sustainable Development Goals Monitoring Framework","Serbia is presently in the process of establishing the institutional framework for monitoring the achievement of sustainable development goals.",""],[1,"7","3","Serbia and 2030 Agenda Reporting and Mapping Exercise","The \"Serbia and 2030 Agenda\" report was updated through the assistance provided under the GIZ Project \"Public Finance Reform - Financ- ing 2030 Agenda\" in 2020.",""],[1,"8","4","Implementation of the Sustainable Development Goals through the EU Integration Process","there is full consensus to implement the sustainable development goals through the EU integration process.",""],[1,"8","5","Integration of the 2030 Agenda into Development Plans and Policy Documents","all development plans and policy documents in the process of Republic of Serbia's EU integration should also integrate the 2030 Agenda",""],[1,"8","5","Nationalisation of Sustainable Development Goals","the \"nationalisation\" of sustainable development goals should follow the same principles and standards established by the EU",""],[1,"8","5","Use of the 2030 Agenda to Support EU Accession Profiling","use it to profile the Republic of Serbia as a future EU member state",""],[1,"8","7","MAPS Joint UN Coordination Approach","a joint approach geared towards more effective and coherent support for the implementation of the 2030 Agenda was adopted in the form of so-called MAPS (Mainstreaming, Acceleration and Policy Support).",""],[1,"85","1","Inter-Sectoral SDG Working Group","In December 2015, the Government established the Inter-sectoral Working Group for Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs) tasked to carry out nationalisation, implementation and monitoring of SDGs in the Republic of Serbia",""],[1,"85","1","Voluntary National Review Preparation","At the meeting held on 1 September 2017, it was agreed that the Repub- lic of Serbia was to start drafting the Voluntary National Review on the Implementation of the Sus- tainable Development Goals.",""],[1,"85","1","First Voluntary National Review Submission","The Republic of Serbia presented its first Voluntary National Review of the Republic of Serbia on the Implementation of the 2030 Agenda for Sustainable Development in July 2019 before the United Nations at the Ministerial Meeting of the High-Level Political Forum on Sustainable Development.",""],[1,"85","3","Integration of the Development Agenda and Reporting Process through the Existing Institutional Framework","the process of prioritisation and nationalisation of the sustainable development goals in the Republic of Serbia opens the possibility to integrate the development agenda and the reporting process through the existent institutional framework, i.e. European Semester light.",""]],"5":[[1,"18","2","Judicial Reform and Case Management Strengthening","Further strengthening of the judiciary and independence of the prosecutor's office, amending the laws on the High Judicial Council and the State Prosecutorial Council, adoption and imple- mentation a human resource strategy for the entire judiciary are necessary, as well as establish- ment of a unified and centralized case management system.",""],[1,"18","4","Strengthening Rule of Law and Access to Justice","Independent judiciary is a precondition for the rule of law, while the state parties are invited to enable access to justice for all.",""],[1,"18","4","Cooperation with the International Criminal Court","The role of Interna- tional Criminal Court is recognised and cooperation with this institution is demanded.",""],[1,"20","6","National Judicial Reform Strategy","National Judicial Reform Strategy for the period from 2020 to 2025 as one of the strategic goals defines strengthening the independence and autonomy of the judiciary, which contributes towards the attainment of the target 16.3 rule of law and equal access to justice for all",""],[1,"20","6","Systemic Free Legal Aid","The Law on Free Legal Aid was adopted on 9 November 2018, and has been implemented since 1 October 2019, enabled to introduce systemic free legal aid.",""],[1,"21","1","Free Legal Aid Provision","the Law on Free Legal Aid, 3,672 request for free legal aid were submitted, and 3,386 or 91% of the requests were granted .",""],[1,"21","1","Municipal Free Legal Aid Service","Municipal service for provision of free legal aid extended the necessary legal aid, and 669 beneficiaries were referred to lawyers.",""],[1,"21","1","Judicial Reform Activities Under Chapter 23 Action Plan","The Action Plan for Negotiating Chap- ter 23 has a separate sub-chapter dedicated to judiciary, envisaging a series of activities serving the same purpose as the National Strategy for Judicial Reform.",""],[1,"21","1","Constitutional Amendments for Judicial Independence","To facilitate these activities in the domain of independent judiciary, some constitutional amendments are also necessary.",""],[1,"87","8","Judicial Development Strategy","New strategies have been adopted in the period from 2020 to 2021: ... development of the judiciary",""]],"6":[[1,"31","4","Water Management Strategy and Action Plan","Water Manage- ment Strategy of the territory of the Republic of Serbia until 2034 was adopted.",""],[1,"55","4","Public Enterprise Restructuring for Water Infrastructure Financing","The most important precondition for the implementation of the Drinking Water Directive and the Urban Wastewater Treatment Directive is the restructuring of public enterprises, improving cost collection and dynamic harmonization of tariffs for financing the work of developed infrastructure.",""],[1,"56","2","Water Framework Directive Implementation","The most important enactment in the field of water is the Water Framework Directive (Directive 2000/60/EC), which is an operational tool for achieving the key objectives of European water policy: comprehensive protection of all waters, taking into account the natural interaction between them in quantitative and qualitative terms, with the application of the principles of integrated water resources management.",""],[1,"56","4","Joint River Basin Measures Programme","Each of the mentioned plans determines the Joint Programme of measures to be implemented in order to improve the state of the environment in the basin.",""],[1,"57","1","Water Management Strategy","The key strategic document in this area is the Water Management Strategy on the territory of the Republic of Serbia until 2034, which is especially related to the implementation of targets 6.1 achieve universal and equal access to safe and affordable drinking water for all, 6.3 im- prove water quality (UN indicator 6.3.1), 6.4 increase water-use efficiency across all sectors (UN indicator 6.4.1), and 6.5 integrated water resources management at all levels.",""],[1,"57","1","Water Management Strategy Action Plan","Action Plan for the Implementation of the Water Management Strategy on the territory of the Republic of Serbia for the period from 2021 to 2023 was also adopted.",""],[1,"87","9","Integrated Water Management Strategy Action Plan","The Action Plan for the implementation of the Integrat- ed Water Management Strategy and two programmes (the Rare Diseases Programme and the Programme for Improving Cancer Screening) were adopted in the period from 2020 to 2021.",""],[1,"98","4","Water Management Strategy and Action Plan","Water Management Strategy of the territory of the Republic of Serbia until 2034 and its accompanying AP for the period 2021 to 2023",""],[1,"102","3","Integrated Water Resources Management and Water Efficiency Measures","Improve water quality (6.3), increase water-use efficiency (6.4), implement integrated water resources manage- ment at all levels (6.5)",""],[1,"102","8","Community Participation in Water and Sanitation Management","Support and strengthen the participation of local commu- nities in water and sanitation management (6.b)",""]],"7":[[1,"31","4","Air Protection Programme","Also, it is planned to adopt new public policy documents for air protec- tion, waste management and land protection (Air Protection Programme, National Programme for Combating Desertification and Land Degradation and Waste Management Programme are under development).",""],[1,"60","5","National Air Quality Improvement Strategy","drafting a strategic document for improving air quality at the national",""],[1,"61","1","National Plan for the Reduction of Main Pollutant Emissions from Old Large Combustion Plants","Currently, this area is largely regulated by National Plan for the Reduction of the Main Pollutant Emissions from Old Large Combustion Plant -NERP.",""],[1,"61","1","Local Air Quality Plans for Polluted Zones and Agglomerations","In zones and agglomerations where the air is of the third category, i.e. when air pollution exceeds the effects of measures taken, i.e. when the capacity of the environment is endangered or there is constant air pollution in a certain area, the competent authority of the autonomous province and local government is obliged to adopt an Air Quality Plan, in order to achieve the appropriate limit values or target values set by applicable regulations.",""],[1,"61","1","Air Protection Programme","The Waste Management Programme (under preparation) and the Air Protection Programme (under preparation) will further contribute to the attainment of this target.",""],[1,"68","1","Air Quality Protection Strategy","Air Quality Protection Strategy (Programme), including aims of UNECE Goteborg protocol and defining long term measures for the reduction of emissions from different sectors relevant to the NEC Directive;",""],[1,"68","2","National Air Pollution Control Programme","National Air Pollution Control Programme - the aim of this national programme will be to limit emissions of certain pollutants of anthropogenic origin in order to achieve defined emission reduction obligations at the national level",""],[1,"88","8","Air Protection Strategy","it is necessary to adopt the National Housing Strategy, Road Traffic Safety Strategy, new Spatial Plan of the Republic of Serbia, Strategy for Cultural Development Strategy, Waste Management Strategy and the Air Protection Strategy.",""],[1,"89","2","Air Protection Strategy","The adoption of the Low Carbon Development Strategy, Programme for Adaptation to Changed Climate Conditions and the Energy and Climate Plan is expected, as well as the beginning of drafting of the Waste Management Strategy, Air Protection Strategy (Programme) and National Air Pollution Control Programme.",""],[1,"89","2","National Air Pollution Control Programme","The adoption of the Low Carbon Development Strategy, Programme for Adaptation to Changed Climate Conditions and the Energy and Climate Plan is expected, as well as the beginning of drafting of the Waste Management Strategy, Air Protection Strategy (Programme) and National Air Pollution Control Programme.",""],[1,"98","4","Air Protection Programme","Air Protection Programme (under preparation)",""],[1,"109","7","National Plan for the Reduction of Main Pollutant Emissions from Old Large Combustion Plants","National Plan for the Reduction of the Main Pollutant Emissions from Old Large Combustion Plant -NERP (in line with the CEC obligations)",""],[1,"109","7","Air Protection Programme","Air Protection Programme (under preparation)",""],[1,"112","4","Air Protection Programme","Air Protection Programme (under preparation);",""]],"8":[[1,"67","6","Low-Carbon Development Strategy and Action Plan","Draft Strategy for Low Carbon Development of the Republic of Serbia for the period from 2021 to 2030 with projections until 2050, along with its accompanying Action Plan for the period from 2021 to 2023 (public consulta- tions finalised), has been prepared, as an umbrella document to combat climate change.",""],[1,"67","6","Programme for Adaptation to Changed Climate Conditions","In addi- tion, the Programme for Adaptation to Changed Climate Conditions is being prepared.",""],[1,"67","6","Greenhouse Gas Reduction Measures","the priority measures for reducing greenhouse gas emissions have been identified.",""],[1,"69","2","Low Carbon Development Strategy Investment Increase","The Low Carbon Development Strategy (public consultation finalised) envisages an increase in investment in order to promote the transition to a climate-neutral economy and a climate-resilient society undertaking obligations from the \"UN Framework Convention on Climate Change\", which is in line with 13.a.",""],[1,"89","2","Low Carbon Development Strategy","The adoption of the Low Carbon Development Strategy, Programme for Adaptation to Changed Climate Conditions and the Energy and Climate Plan is expected, as well as the beginning of drafting of the Waste Management Strategy, Air Protection Strategy (Programme) and National Air Pollution Control Programme.",""],[1,"89","2","Programme for Adaptation to Changed Climate Conditions","The adoption of the Low Carbon Development Strategy, Programme for Adaptation to Changed Climate Conditions and the Energy and Climate Plan is expected, as well as the beginning of drafting of the Waste Management Strategy, Air Protection Strategy (Programme) and National Air Pollution Control Programme.",""],[1,"89","2","Energy and Climate Plan","The adoption of the Low Carbon Development Strategy, Programme for Adaptation to Changed Climate Conditions and the Energy and Climate Plan is expected, as well as the beginning of drafting of the Waste Management Strategy, Air Protection Strategy (Programme) and National Air Pollution Control Programme.",""],[1,"112","4","Initial National Climate Change Communication","Initial National Communication on Climate Change - UNFCCC",""],[1,"112","4","First Biannual Updated Climate Change Report","First Biannual Updated Report (FBUR) in accordance with the UN Framework Convention on Climate Change - UNFCCC",""],[1,"112","4","Second National Climate Change Communication","Second national communication to the United Nations Framework Convention on Climate Change - UNFCCC",""],[1,"112","4","Low Carbon Development Strategy","Low Carbon Development Strate- gy (public debate completed);",""],[1,"112","4","Sectoral Adaptation Programmes for Changed Climatic Conditions","Programmes of Adaptation to Changed Climatic Conditions by Sectors (under preparation, IPA 2016)",""],[1,"112","6","Integration of Climate Change Measures into National Policies and Strategies","Integrate climate change measures into national poli- cies and strategies (13.2)",""]],"9":[[1,"70","4","Invasive Alien Species Prevention and Risk Management Measures","It is necessary to introduce measures to prevent the introduction and significantly reduce the impact of invasive alien species on land and water ecosystems (15.8).",""],[1,"70","5","Integration of Ecosystem and Biodiversity Values into Planning","Integrate ecosystem and biodiversity values into national and local planning (15.9)",""],[1,"70","6","Biodiversity and Ecosystem Conservation Financing Mobilization","It is necessary to mobilize and increase financial resources from all sources to conserve and sustainably use biodiversity and ecosystems, as well as to finance sustainable forest manage- ment (15.a and 15.b).",""],[1,"71","1","EU 2030 Biodiversity Strategy","The EU 2030 Biodiversity Strategy sets it basis on the four pillars of equal importance: 1. Na- ture protection (extension of the coverage of protected areas to the level of 30% in the EU), 2. Restoration of nature (establishment of sustainable management in all sectors and ecosystems), 3. Transformation (improvement of the legislative framework and promotion of investments) 4. Strengthening biodiversity at the global level (supporting the strengthening of biodiversity out- side the EU).",""],[1,"71","4","Nature Protection Programme 2021-2023","Nature Protection Programme of the Republic of Serbia for the period from 2021 to 2023 with the accompanying Action Plan prescribes the need for nature conservation and biodiversity conservation, which is in accordance with target 15.1.",""],[1,"72","3","Nature Protection Programme and Action Plan","In order to achieve continuity in nature protection and biodiversity, the Nature Protection Programme of the Republic of Serbia for the period from 2021 to 2023 with the accompanying Action Plan for the period from 2021 to 2023, was adopted.",""],[1,"72","4","Programme for Nature Conservation of the Republic of Serbia","Programme for Nature Conservation of the Republic of Serbia for the period from 2021 to 2023 and the accompanying AP for the period from 2021 to 2023",""],[1,"73","1","Nature Conservation Financing Framework","Programme for Nature Conservation of the Republic of Serbia for the period from 2021 to 2023, with its accompanying Action Plan, defines financial framework for nature conservation.",""],[1,"113","13","Nature Conservation Programme and Action Plan 2021-2023","Programme for Nature Conser- vation of the Republic of Serbia for the period from 2021 to 2023 and the accompanying AP for the period from 2021 to 2023",""],[1,"113","16","Nature Conservation Programme and Action Plan 2021-2023","Programme for Nature Conser- vation of the Republic of Serbia for the period from 2021 to 2023 and the accompanying AP for the period from 2021 to 2023",""],[1,"114","5","End Poaching and Trafficking of Protected Species","End poaching and trafficking of protected species of flora and fauna (15.7)",""],[1,"114","6","Nature Conservation Programme and Action Plan 2021-2023","Programme for Nature Conser- vation of the Republic of Serbia for the period from 2021 to 2023 and the accompanying AP for the period from 2021 to 2023",""],[1,"114","9","Nature Conservation Programme and Action Plan","Programme for Nature Conser- vation of the Republic of Serbia for the period from 2021 to 2023 and the accompanying AP for the period from 2021 to 2023",""],[1,"114","15","Nature Conservation Programme and Action Plan 2021-2023","Programme for Nature Conser- vation of the Republic of Serbia for the period from 2021 to 2023 and the accompanying AP for the period from 2021 to 2023",""]],"10":[[1,"33","4","European Pillar of Social Rights Action Plan","in 2021 the European Pillar of Social Rights Action Plan was adopted.",""],[1,"33","4","European Platform Against Poverty","The European Platform against Poverty includes taking a number of measures within public policies, greater and more successful use of EU funds to support social inclusion, promote social innovation, work through partnerships and exploit the potential of the social economy and improve coordination between countries.",""],[1,"34","3","Employment and Social Reform Programme","The Employment and Social Reform Programme in the Process of Accession to the European Union (ESRP) is one of the most important documents for the attainment of the SDG 1.",""],[1,"34","4","New Social Protection Strategy","A draft of the new Social Protection Strategy of the Republic of Serbia has been prepared and is expected to the adopted.",""],[1,"35","3","Improved Targeting of Social Assistance Programmes","There is a trend of improving the social component of the budget by better targeting social assistance programmes and increasing allocations for health and educa- tion functions.",""],[1,"89","3","Umbrella Hunger Reduction Strategy","An appropriate umbrella strategy should be adopted so as to tackle hunger in a systematic way.",""],[1,"89","3","Poverty Reduction Strategy","The adoption of a Poverty Reduction Strategy would significantly contribute to defining a long-term policy to reduce hunger.",""]],"11":[[1,"23","1","Gender Equality in Political Participation Strategy","The Strategy for Gender Equality for the period from 2021 to 2030 (no accompanying AP) defines the strengthening of gender equality in political life and ensuring equal participation of women and men in decision-making on public affairs.",""],[1,"37","1","Legal Framework for Women's Equal Economic Rights","there is an improvement in the legal framework that enables women equal rights to economic resources, as well as access to ownership and control over land and oth- er forms of property, financial services, heritage and natural resources",""],[1,"37","3","Gender Equality Strategy 2020-2025","At the EU level, the Gender equality Strategy for the period from 2020 to 2025 strives for ex- ercising freedom of choice, equal opportunities for progress and equal participation in the de- cision-making of men and women.",""],[1,"37","4","Gender Equality Strategy 2021-2030","Gender Equality Strategy for the period from 2021 to 2030 (no accompanying AP) is crucial for the attainment of the SDG 5, as well as for strengthening the capacity of institutions and organiza- tions, improving the coordination of key actors and raising citizens' awareness of gender equality.",""],[1,"49","3","Gender Equality Law Implementation","The adopted Law on Gender Equality will further contribute to the improvement of the position of women.",""],[1,"88","1","Gender Equality Strategy 2021-2030","the Gender Equality Strategy for the period from 2021 to 2030 (adopted in 2021) is an umbrella strategy.",""],[1,"100","4","Gender Equality Strategy","Strategy for Gender Equality for the period 2021 to 2030 (no accompanying AP)",""],[1,"116","11","Strategy for Gender Equality","Strategy for Gender Equality for the period from 2021 to 2030 (no accompanying AP)",""]],"12":[[1,"42","2","Education Development Strategy and Action Plan","The most important strategic document of the Republic of Serbia for the attainment of the SDG 4 is the Strategy for the Development of Education of the Republic of Serbia until 2030 with its accompanying Action Plan for the period from 2021 to 2023, which was adopted in 2021.",""],[1,"42","3","Education Quality Standards and Curriculum Improvement Strategy","The priorities of the Strategy in this area are the development of new and improvement of existing qualification and achievement standards, improvement of teaching and learning programmes, support in strengthening the educational function, improvement of self-evaluation and external evaluation of institutions and systems and processes for monitoring student progress and new curricula.",""],[1,"42","6","Higher Education Quality Monitoring and Policy Framework","The vital for this goal is the development of a framework for monitoring and evaluating the quality of higher education and the application of the results obtained in the formulation of higher education policy, as well as other measures envisaged by the strategy: improving the financing system, strengthening human capacities and increasing the level of cooperation at the national and international level.",""],[1,"49","4","Education Quality and Access Improvement Action Plan","The initiatives launched under the Strategy for the Development of Education in the Republic of Serbia until 2030 with the Ac- tion Plan for the period from 2021 to 2023 which, among other things, aims to improve the quality and access to all levels of education, are extremely important.",""],[1,"100","4","Education Development Strategy","Strategy for the Development of Education in the Republic of Serbia until 2030 and the accompanying AP for the period from 2021 to 2023",""]],"13":[[1,"42","4","Early Childhood Education Access and Preschool Capacity Expansion","The Strategy defines measures and activities aimed at educating teaching staff, developing and strengthening the network of pedagogical assistants in preschool institutions, establishing a repository with materials for practice in preschool institutions and increasing the number of preschool institutions and their coverage.",""]],"14":[[1,"42","6","Qualifications Agency Operational Support","Necessary conditions were ensured for the smooth functioning of the Qualifications Agency during 2019.",""]],"15":[[1,"41","3","Skills Agenda and Education and Training Support","Through the Skills Agenda , the Strategic Framework for Education and Training and through Erasmus+ programme , Europe directly supports the improvement of education and training in its Member States.",""],[1,"41","7","Erasmus+ Programme Participation","Serbia has been a full member of the Erasmus + programme since 2019 and has the status of a programme country, which means that institutions and organizations can apply for all types of projects, as well as EU member states .",""],[1,"42","6","Secondary Vocational Education Reform Plan","The action plan in the field of secondary vocational education envisages the improvement of curricula, introduction of new profiles, involvement of employers in the process of developing this level of education and monitoring and evaluation of students.",""],[1,"42","7","Dual and Entrepreneurial Education Programme","Due to the mismatch of labour force qualifications with the needs of the labour market, the concept of dual and entrepreneurial education was introduced.",""]],"16":[[1,"48","1","Public Research System Improvement Strategy","The basis of this Strategy is to improve the quality and efficiency of science, technological development and innovation through the development of excellence and relevance of scientific research, as well as strengthening the connection between science, economy and society.",""],[1,"48","1","Research Alignment with Societal Priorities and International Cooperation","Focusing research on societal challenges and priorities and strengthening international cooperation further encourages economic growth.",""],[1,"54","3","Scientific and Technological Development Strategy 2021-2025","Target 9.5 enhance scientific research, upgrade the technological capabilities and encour- aging innovation is covered by the Scientific and Technological Development Strategy of the Republic of Serbia for the period from 2021 to 2025 with the accompanying AP for the pe- riod from 2021 to 2023",""],[1,"54","3","Increase Investment in Science and Research","elements of the Strategy related to increasing investments in the science and research",""],[1,"54","3","Strengthen Science-Economy Linkages","strengthening the links between science and the economy",""],[1,"54","3","Develop Scientific Infrastructure and Staff","developing scientific infrastructure and staff",""]],"17":[[1,"46","5","EU Sustainable Development Promotion Agenda","One of the priorities of the new strategic agenda of the EU for the period from 2019 to 2024 is to respond to global challenges by promoting sustainable development, which is a direct response of the European Union to the Sustainable Development Goal 8.",""],[1,"48","3","Industrial Policy Strategy for Entrepreneurship Promotion","The following strategic documents contribute towards the development of entrepreneurship: Industrial Policy Strategy of the Republic of Serbia for the period from 2021 to 2030 and the accompanying AP for the period from 2021 to 2023 through mechanisms for encouraging and promoting entrepreneurship",""],[1,"48","3","Free Zone Development Strategy","Free Zone Development Strategy of the Republic of Serbia for the period from 2018 to 2022 with the accompanying AP for the period from 2018 to 2022 by strengthening production capacities and encouraging exports within free zones",""],[1,"48","3","Doing Business Improvement Programme","Additional contribution to the improvement of the business environment is provided by measures and activities defined within the Programme for Improving the Position of the Republic of Serbia on the Doing Business List of the World Bank for the period from 2020 to 2023 with the AP for the period from 2020 to 2023",""],[1,"48","3","National Programme for Suppression of the Grey Economy","National Programme for the Suppression of the Grey Economy in the Republic of Serbia for the period from 2021 to 2025 is under development",""],[1,"49","3","Social Entrepreneurship Regulatory Reform","Additional conditions for achieving target 8.5 will be provided by improving the regulatory framework for social entrepreneurship, which is recognized as one of the measures under this Strategy.",""],[1,"50","3","SME Financial Literacy and Banking Access Programmes","there are various programmes of the National Bank of Serbia and the Ministry of Economy to increase SME financial literacy or improve access to banking services.","National Bank of Serbia | Ministry of Economy"],[1,"50","3","Microfinance Institutional and Legal Framework","One of the key steps that will contribute to the achievement of this target in the future will be the establishment of the institutional and legal framework for microfinance that is expected in the coming period.",""],[1,"51","4","Expand Funding Sources for Innovative and Start-Up Companies","The scope of funding sources for innovative and start-up companies in the form of venture capital funds and other instruments needs to be expanded.",""],[1,"53","6","SME Value Chain Integration and Financial Support Measures","Programmes for the integration of SMEs into value chains, as well as other measures of financial support, are implemented by the Development Agency of Serbia and other state institutions.",""]],"18":[[1,"50","5","Road Network Construction and Local Road Improvement","In addition to the construction of key sections on Corridors X and XI, the network of local roads is continuously improving, which contributes to the growth of freight and passenger transport (3.1 billion passenger km and 7.7 billion tonne-kilometres in 2020).",""],[1,"50","5","Railway Network Reconstruction","Reconstruction of the existing railway network (especially the Belgrade-Budapest railway) has limited the volume of railway traffic in 2020.",""],[1,"52","5","Sustainable and Smart Mobility Strategy","the Sustainable and Smart Mobility Strategy has been adopted",""],[1,"53","3","National Transport Strategy 2022-2030","The preparation of the new National Transport Strategy for the period from 2022 to 2030 is underway.",""],[1,"59","3","Road Traffic Safety Strategy","Target 11.2 sustainable transport systems and road safety was implemented through the Road Traffic Safety Strategy in the period from 2015 to 2020 aiming to reduce mortality rate and heavy injury risk.",""],[1,"59","3","Law on Road Traffic Safety","After the expiry of the mentioned Strategy, only the Law on Road Traffic Safety regulates road traffic safety.",""],[1,"59","3","Strategy on Development of Waterborne Transport","In water transport, the development of the transport system and increasing the level of safety are contained in the Strategy on Development of Waterborne Transport of the Republic of Serbia for the period from 2015 to 2025 (accompanying AP has expired),",""],[1,"59","3","National Programme for Public Rail Infrastructure","while in railway transport it is defined through the National Programme for Public Rail Infrastructure in the Republic of Serbia for the period 2017 to 2021 (no accompanying AP).",""],[1,"81","1","Western Balkans Transport Infrastructure Cooperation and TEN-T Extension","The aim of the SEETO is to promote co- operation on the construction of the main and secondary transport infrastructure in the region in accordance with the indicative extension of the TEN-T network for the Western Balkans.",""],[1,"81","1","Soft Measures Framework for Transport Infrastructure Financing","The European Commission provides a framework for financing infrastructure, which is conditioned by adoption and implementation of the so-called \"soft measures\", while the Energy Community Secretariat deals with defining these soft measures and monitoring.",""],[1,"88","5","Public Rail Infrastructure Programme","Continuity in the development and improvement of transport infrastructure (SDG 9) is defined through the Strategy on Development of Waterborne Transport and Programme for Public Rail Infrastructure.",""],[1,"88","5","National Transport Strategy","The adoption of the National Transport Strategy is of great importance for further strengthening the transport infrastructure.",""]],"19":[[1,"52","8","Broadband Network Introduction Technical Assistance","the EU has also increased technical assistance for the introduc- tion of broadband networks in the region.",""],[1,"54","5","Digital Agenda for Information Society and Information Security","Strategy for the Development of the Information Society and Information Security in the Republic of Serbia for the period from 2021 to 2026 with the accompanying Action Plan for the period from 2021 to 2023 constitutes the Digital Agenda of the Republic of Serbia.",""],[1,"54","5","Digital Skills Development Strategy","the Strategy for the Development of Digital Skills in the Republic of Serbia for the period from 2020 to 2024 (no accompanying AP)",""],[1,"54","5","New Generation Networks Development Strategy","the Strategy for the Development of New Generation Networks until 2023 (no accompanying AP) contributes to achieving the goal of 9.c increase access to information and communications technology.",""],[1,"54","5","Broadband Infrastructure Improvement Investments","Other activities and investments are planned to improve broadband infrastructure.",""],[1,"82","6","Enabling Technology and ICT Enhancement","Enhance the use of enabling technology and ICT (17.8) has a high level of priority within the following strategic documents: Strategy for the Development of the Artificial Intelligence in the Republic of Serbia for the period from 2020 to 2025 (accompanying AP for the period from 2020 to 2022) and Scientific and Technological Development Strategy of the Republic of Serbia for the period from 2021 to 2025 \"The Power of Knowledge\" (accompanying AP for the period from 2021 to 2023).",""]],"20":[[1,"53","4","Energy Sector Development Strategy","The strategic framework document in the area of energy is the Energy Sector Development Strategy of the Republic of Serbia until 2025, with projections until 2030 .",""],[1,"53","4","Energy Strategy Implementation Programme","Conditions, manner, dynamics and measures for the implementation of the Energy Strategy are determined by the Programme for the Implementation of the Energy Development Strategy of the Republic of Serbia until 2025 with projections until 2030, for the period from 2017 to 2023 .",""],[1,"54","2","Energy Sector Development Strategy Implementation","The implementation of the above- mentioned Energy Sector Development Strategy is also highly relevant to the achievement of this target.",""],[1,"58","2","Energy Development Strategy Implementation Programme","Conditions, manner, dynamics and measures for the implementation of this Strategy are determined by the Programme for the Implementation of the Energy Development Strategy of the Republic of Serbia until 2025 with projections until 2030, for the period from 2017 to 2023.",""],[1,"58","3","Renewable Energy Sources Promotion Framework","The Law on the Use of Renewable Energy Sources encourages the production and consumption of electricity from large and small watercourses, wind and solar energy, the production and consumption of thermal energy from geothermal energy and solid biomass.",""],[1,"58","5","Biomass and Geothermal Energy Use in Heating Plants","The largest scope of cooperation refers to the use of biomass and geothermal energy sources in heating plants.",""],[1,"58","7","Adoption of Energy Sector Legal and Regulatory Amendments","new or harmonized laws and bylaws (Amendments to the Law on Energy, Law on Energy Efficiency and Rational Use of Energy and the Law on the Use of Renewable Energy Sources) were adopted",""],[1,"66","2","Energy Efficiency and Renewable Energy Measures","The Energy Community of South East Europe, of which Serbia is a member, steers the implementation of measures aimed at energy efficiency and use of renewables as well as the fulfilment of obligations arising from the Kyoto Protocol.",""],[1,"68","7","Comprehensive Sustainable Energy Transition Strategy","This Strategy identifies as one of the three priorities a comprehensive transition to sustainable energy, through the improvement of energy efficiency in performing energy activities and energy consumption; increasing the share of energy from renewable energy sources and improving the state and systems of environmental protection in all areas of energy activities.",""],[1,"68","8","Energy Efficiency and Renewable Energy Measures","In addition to the measures and activities taken from the AP for energy efficiency and the AP for the use of renewable energy sources, additional measures and activities are included in order to improve the situation in the areas of renewable energy sources and energy efficiency.",""],[1,"88","7","Energy Development Strategy","Energy Development Strategy until 2025 with projections until 2030 is an umbrella document which, among other things, is a framework for providing affordable energy to all citizens, encouraging the participation of renewable energy sources in total production and con- sumption and strengthening institutional capacity to achieve energy efficiency.",""],[1,"102","13","Energy Development Strategy and Implementation Programme","Energy Development Strategy until 2025 with the Projections until 2030 and the Energy Development Strategy Implementation Programme from 2017 to 2023",""],[1,"103","7","Energy Development Strategy and Implementation Programme","Energy Development Strategy until 2025 with the Projections until 2030 and the Energy Development Strategy Implementation Programme from 2017 to 2023",""],[1,"103","7","National Energy and Climate Plan","Energy and Climate Plan of the Republic of Serbia from 2021 to 2030 with the vision until 2050 (obligation in line with the CEC, under development)",""],[1,"106","7","Energy Development Strategy and Implementation Programme","Energy Development Strategy until 2025 with the Projections until 2030 and the Energy Development Strategy Implementation Programme from 2017 to 2023",""],[1,"110","8","Energy Development Strategy and Implementation Programme","Energy Development Strategy of the Republic of Serbia until 2025 with the Projections until 2030 and the Energy Develop- ment Strategy Implementation Programme from 2017 to 2023",""],[1,"112","7","Energy Development Strategy and Implementation Programme","Energy Development Strategy until 2025 with the Projections until 2030 and the Energy De- velopment Strategy Implemen- tation Programme from 2017 to 2023",""],[1,"112","7","Energy and Climate Plan","Energy and Climate Plan of the Republic of Serbia from 2021 to 2030 with the vision until 2050 (obligation in line with the CEC, under development)",""]],"21":[[1,"60","3","Strategy for Cultural Development 2020-2029","The Strategy for Cultural Development from 2020 to 2029 was adopted by the Government and sent to the National Assembly for its adoption, but it was returned to the new procedure.",""],[1,"60","3","Integrated Protection of Cultural and Natural Heritage","The envisaged measures (contained in the Strategy for Cultural Development), among other things, relate to the integrated protection of cultural and natural heritage",""],[1,"88","3","Strategy for Cultural Development","In the coming period, the Strategy for Cultural Development and the Strategy for Supporting the Development of Small and Medium Enterprises should be adopted along with the setting of the institutional and legal framework for microfinance.",""],[1,"88","8","Strategy for Cultural Development","it is necessary to adopt the National Housing Strategy, Road Traffic Safety Strategy, new Spatial Plan of the Republic of Serbia, Strategy for Cultural Development Strategy, Waste Management Strategy and the Air Protection Strategy.",""]],"22":[[1,"31","4","Waste Management Programme","Also, it is planned to adopt new public policy documents for air protec- tion, waste management and land protection (Air Protection Programme, National Programme for Combating Desertification and Land Degradation and Waste Management Programme are under development).",""],[1,"60","5","New Waste Management Policy Document","A new policy document for waste manage- ment is being drafted",""],[1,"61","1","Waste Management Programme","The Waste Management Programme (under preparation) and the Air Protection Programme (under preparation) will further contribute to the attainment of this target.",""],[1,"62","5","Waste Prevention, Recycling, and Reuse Programme","Generated waste should be substantially reduced through prevention, reduction, recycling and reuse (12.5).",""],[1,"62","6","Regional Sanitary Landfill Construction Programme","The closure and reclamation of existing landfills and the construction of 29 regional sanitary landfills are planned.",""],[1,"62","6","Landfill Closure and Reclamation Programme","The closure and reclamation of existing landfills and the construction of 29 regional sanitary landfills are planned.",""],[1,"62","7","Local and Regional Waste Management Planning","Each local self-government had the obligation to develop a local waste management plan, and each region was obliged to develop a regional waste management plan.",""],[1,"62","7","Sanitary Landfill Waste Disposal","Although they have the obligation to dispose of waste in sanitary landfills, local self-government units fail to do that.",""],[1,"63","3","Local and Regional Waste Management Planning","Each local self-government has the obligation to develop a local waste management plan, and each region, a regional waste management plan.",""],[1,"63","6","Circular Economy Package","The transition to an improved circular economy in the EU is being materialised through the so- called \"Circular Economy Package\" adopted by the European Commission in late 2015.",""],[1,"63","7","EU Waste Framework Directive Implementation","EU Waste Framework Directive is of immense importance along with its two key objectives: prevention and reduction of adverse impact resulting from waste generation and management and improvement of resource efficiency.",""],[1,"68","3","Waste Management Strategy and Integrated National Waste Management Plan","Waste Management Strategy (Programme), with integrated National Waste Management Plan, as well as Hazardous Waste Management Plan and Waste Sludge Management Plan;",""],[1,"68","4","National Biodegradable Waste Reduction Strategy","Development of the National Strategy for the Reduction of Biodegradable Waste disposed of in landfills and incorporation of the Strategy into the National Waste Management Plan",""],[1,"88","8","Waste Management Strategy","it is necessary to adopt the National Housing Strategy, Road Traffic Safety Strategy, new Spatial Plan of the Republic of Serbia, Strategy for Cultural Development Strategy, Waste Management Strategy and the Air Protection Strategy.",""],[1,"89","2","Waste Management Strategy","The adoption of the Low Carbon Development Strategy, Programme for Adaptation to Changed Climate Conditions and the Energy and Climate Plan is expected, as well as the beginning of drafting of the Waste Management Strategy, Air Protection Strategy (Programme) and National Air Pollution Control Programme.",""],[1,"98","4","Waste Management Programme","Waste Management Pro- gramme (under preparation)",""],[1,"104","7","Waste Management Programme","Waste Management Programme (under development)",""],[1,"109","7","Waste Management Programme","Waste Management Pro- gramme (under preparation)",""],[1,"110","8","Circular Economy Programme","Circular Economy Programme (under development).",""],[1,"111","4","Waste Management Programme","Waste Management Pro- gramme (under preparation);",""],[1,"111","7","Waste Management Programme","Waste Management Pro- gramme (under preparation);",""]],"23":[[1,"82","1","Sava River Basin Flood Protection Protocol","Special Pro- tocol on Flood Protection to the Framework Agreement, ratification of which is in progress, will regulate the cooperation in order to prevent and/or reduce the risk of flooding, by undertaking appropriate measures and activities.",""],[1,"109","4","National Disaster Risk Management Programme","National Disaster Risk Manage- ment Programme (not time- bound, without accompanying AP from 2020)",""],[1,"109","4","National Strategy for Protection and Rescue in the State of Emergency","National Strategy for Protec- tion and Rescue in the State of Emergency (not time-bound and no accompanying AP)",""],[1,"112","4","National Strategy for Protection and Rescue in State of Emergency","National Strategy for Protec- tion and Rescue in the State of Emergency (not time-bound, no accompanying AP).",""],[1,"112","4","National Disaster Risk Management Programme","National Disaster Risk Manage- ment Programme (not time- bound, without accompanying AP)",""]],"24":[[1,"82","8","Regulatory Reform and Public Policy Management Programme","Regulatory Reform and Public Policy Management Programme for the period from 2021 to 2025 (in the adoption procedure) defines effective coordination of public policies and improvement of the planning framework at all levels of government, thus contributing to progress in achieving",""],[1,"89","4","Public Policy Management and Regulatory Reform Programme","Programme for Improving Public Policy Management and Regulatory Reform for the period from 2021 to 2025 (adoption procedure in progress) will be of great importance for improving coordination and coher- ence in public policy-making.",""],[1,"116","11","Public Policy Management and Regulatory Reform Programme","Programme for Improving Public Policy Management and Regulatory Reform for the period from 2021 to 2025 (public hearing completed).",""],[1,"120","7","Public Policy Management and Regulatory Reform Programme","Programme for Improving Public Policy Management and Regulatory Reform for the period from 2021 to 2025 (under the adoption procedure)",""],[1,"120","10","Public Policy Management and Regulatory Reform Programme","Programme for Improving and Regulatory Reform for the period from 2021 to 2025 (public hearing completed).",""]],"25":[[1,"87","8","Public Administration Reform","New strategies have been adopted in the period from 2020 to 2021: ... public administration reforms",""],[1,"87","8","E-Government Development Programme","The programmes adopted in the period from 2020 to 2021 additionally contributed to the attainment of the goals within the Fundamentals: Public Finance Management Reform, e-Government Development and Tax Administration Transforma- tion.",""],[1,"116","6","Public Administration Reform Strategy","Public Administration Reform Strategy of the Republic of Ser- bia for the period from 2021 to 2030 and the accompanying AP for the period from 2021 to 2025",""],[1,"116","8","Public Administration Reform Strategy","Public Administration Reform Strategy of the Republic of Serbia for the period from 2021 to 2030 and the accompanying AP for the period from 2021 to 2025",""]],"26":[[1,"87","9","Rare Diseases Programme","The Action Plan for the implementation of the Integrat- ed Water Management Strategy and two programmes (the Rare Diseases Programme and the Programme for Improving Cancer Screening) were adopted in the period from 2020 to 2021.",""],[1,"87","9","Cancer Screening Improvement Programme","The Action Plan for the implementation of the Integrat- ed Water Management Strategy and two programmes (the Rare Diseases Programme and the Programme for Improving Cancer Screening) were adopted in the period from 2020 to 2021.",""],[1,"87","9","Health Care Development Strategy","In the next period, it is expected that the adoption of the umbrella Strategy for the Development of Health Care optimise planning framework in the area of planning.",""],[1,"87","9","Non-Communicable Chronic Diseases Programme","Programme for Non-Communicable Chronic Diseases that would integrate existing documents for certain diseases and factors that affect the occurrence of these diseases (mental health, fight against alcohol dependence, overweight, etc.) should be adopted.",""],[1,"101","4","National Program for Preservation and Improvement of Sexual and Reproductive Health","National Program for Preserva- tion and Improvement of Sexual and Reproductive Health of Cit- izens of the Republic of Serbia (not time-bound, no accompa- nying AP)",""]],"27":[[1,"29","3","EU Health Programme 2021-2027","EU Health Programme for the period 2021-2027 represents a set of measures and activities to im- prove the quality and resilience of health systems, especially in times of health crises.",""],[1,"30","2","HIV and AIDS Prevention and Control Strategy","the Strategy for HIV and AIDS Prevention and Control for the Period from 2018 to 2025 with the accompanying Action Plan for the period from 2018 to 2021 has been adopted.",""],[1,"30","2","Environment and Health Programme","the Environment and Health Programme is being prepared.",""],[1,"30","2","Communicable Diseases Control Programme","Continuation of work on the new health care development strategy will create conditions for the development of a programme that would unite the fight against communicable diseases, with emphasis on strengthening the readiness of the health system for rapid identification of new causes and responses to protect the population.",""],[1,"30","6","National Programme for the Control of Antibiotic Resistance","National Programme for the Control of Bacterial Resistance to Antibiotics for the period 2019 to 2021 with its accompanying Action Plan should ensure the safety of antibiotic use",""],[1,"87","9","Infectious Diseases Combat Programme","In addition, the Programme for Combating Infectious Diseases should be ad- opted, for it is crucial to raising the country's readiness to counter a new threat posed by new viruses.",""],[1,"87","9","Environment and Health Programme","Also, the adoption of the Environment and Health Programme would contribute to the harmoniza- tion of these strategically important areas.",""]],"28":[[1,"104","4","Grey Economy Suppression Programme","National Programme for the Suppression of the Grey Economy in the Republic of Serbia for the Period from 2021 to 2025 (under development)",""]],"29":[[1,"118","9","Fiscal Strategy 2022","Fiscal Strategy for 2022 with projections for 2023 and 2024",""],[1,"119","7","Fiscal Strategy 2022","Fiscal Strategy for 2022 with projections for 2023 and 2024",""],[1,"120","7","Fiscal Strategy","Fiscal Strategy for 2022 with projections for 2023 and 2024",""]],"30":[[1,"58","4","Integrated Energy and Climate Plan to 2030","The Integrated Plan for Energy and Climate until 2030 (under development) ... will define a set of measures that will contribute to improving energy efficiency decree",""],[1,"58","4","Long-Term Strategy for Renovating the National Building Fund","The Long-Term Strategy for Encouraging Investments in the Renovation of the National Building Fund of the Republic of Serbia (under development) will define a set of measures that will contribute to improving energy efficiency decree",""],[1,"69","1","Energy and Climate Plan Development","Drafting of the Energy and Climate Plan for the period 2021-2030 with a vision until 2050 is in progress.",""]],"31":[[1,"25","1","Health Information System and E-Health Expansion","This is attributed to the introduction of a new information system that should lead to a reduction in waiting lists and waiting times, as well as due to investment in radiation therapy and MR scanners and the introduction of e-Prescrip- tions.",""]],"32":[[1,"7","2","National Citizen Consultation Campaign on Development Priorities","Through the national campaign \"The Serbia We Want\", as part of the global campaign \"The World We Want\", over 250,000 citizens became aware of the consultation process concerning the post-2015 period.",""],[1,"23","4","Open Government Partnership Implementation Action Plan","Action plan for the implementation of the Open Government Partnership Initiative in the Republic of Serbia for the period from 2020 to 2022 endeavours to improve the integrity, trans- parency, efficiency and accountability of public authorities, through building public trust, coop- eration with civil society organisations, strengthening citizen participation in governance, fight- ing corruption, access to information, use of new technologies, and in connection with achieving more effective and more responsible work of public authority.",""]],"33":[[1,"8","6","Development Partner Support for SDG-Related Reforms","it is ex- pected that the support the Republic of Serbia receives from it, together with bilateral partners, will continue to support the implementation of reforms leading to the attainment of sustainable development goals.",""]],"34":[[1,"12","34","Strategy Against Money Laundering and Terrorism Financing","Strategy Against Money Laundering and Terrorism Financing for the period from 2020 to 2024",""],[1,"21","3","National Anti-Money Laundering and Counter-Terrorism Financing Strategy","Strategy Against Money Laundering and Terrorism Financing for the period from 2020 to 2025 with the accompanying AP for the period from 2020 to 2022 intends to further develop the system to combat money laundering and terrorism financing in the Republic of Serbia to successfully confront all risks determined in 2018 in the Money Laundering Risk Assessment and Terrorism Financing Risk Assessment.",""],[1,"21","3","Law on Prevention of Money Laundering and Terrorist Financing","The new Law on Prevention of Money Laundering and Terrorist Financing was adopted on 26 December 2020 in order to improve the existing system of detection and prevention of money laundering and terrorist financing and harmonization with European directives in this area.",""],[1,"24","1","Anti-Money Laundering and Counter-Terrorism Financing Strategy","Strategy Against Money Laundering and Terrorism Financing for the period from 2020 to 2024 (with the accompanying AP for the period from 2020 to 2022)",""]],"35":[[1,"12","43","Aarhus Convention Implementation Strategy","Strategy for Implementing the Convention on Access to Information, Public Participation in Decision-making and Access to Justice in Environmental Matters - The Aarhus Convention",""]],"36":[[1,"14","4","Integrated Response to Violence Against Women and Girls","The project \"Integrated Response to Violence Against Women and Girls\" signed between Ser- bia and the UN (related to the target 16.3 rule of law and equal access to justice and indicator 16.1.3) was successfully implemented in the period from 2016 to 2020.",""],[1,"19","2","Transposition of the CAHVIO Convention into National Legislation","The next step should be transposition of the CAHVIO into national legislation and improvement of the position of women victims of violence, as well as criminal prosecution of the perpetrators.",""],[1,"20","2","Strategy for Preventing and Combating Gender-Based Violence and Domestic Violence","Strategy for Preventing and Combating Gender-Based Violence against Women and Domes- tic Violence for the period from 2021 to 2025 with the accompanying Action Plan for the period from 2021 to 2023 provides for elimination of all forms of domestic violence (particularly against women and girls), along with provision of adequate protection and support.",""],[1,"20","2","Domestic Violence Prevention and Protection Measures","Goals defined under this Strategy relate to the improvement of prevention, provision of more efficient and effective protection and support, creation of conditions for adequate prosecution and punishment of per- petrators, improvement of the position of victims and witnesses and establishment of a compre- hensive and functional data collection and analysis system.",""],[1,"24","1","Gender-Based Violence and Domestic Violence Prevention Strategy","Strategy for Preventing and Combating Gender-Based Violence Against Wom- en and Domestic Violence for the period from 2021 to 2025 (with the accompanying AP for the period from 2021 to 2023)",""],[1,"37","5","Strategy for Preventing and Combating Gender-Based Violence and Domestic Violence","Strategy for Preventing and Combating Gender-Based Violence Against Women and Domestic Violence for the period from 2021 to 2025 (the accompanying AP for the period from 2021 to 2023)",""],[1,"36","3","Elimination of Harmful Practices Against Women and Girls","Eliminate all harmful practices, such as child, early and forced marriage and female genital mutilation (5.3) which further disadvantage women and girls.",""]],"37":[[1,"15","5","Institutional Efficiency and Information Exchange for Organized Crime Control","The most important activities in the fight against organized crime (16.4), according to the Ac- tion Plan for Chapter 24 , are increasing the efficiency of competent institutions, improving re- cord keeping and information exchange at national and international level and further promoting regional and international cooperation through regional and international projects.",""],[1,"15","5","Proactive Investigation and Inter-Agency Coordination","One of the recommendations of the AP, important for monitoring and reporting on the attained targets for SDG 16, is to conduct investigations before and during the commission of the crime (proactive in- vestigation), involve state authorities in the earliest stages of the procedure through information exchange and improve coordination, communication and exchange of information among state authorities.",""],[1,"15","5","IT Systems Interoperability and Capacity-Building Programme","It is necessary to continue improving the interoperability of IT systems and strength- ening human capacity through training programmes.",""],[1,"15","5","Uniform Crime Statistics and Data Consolidation System","Establishing uniform statistics for record- ing crimes at the level of police, prosecutor's offices, prisons and courts and consolidating these data are key in the fight against organized crime.",""],[1,"18","1","Single Information System for Criminal Case Monitoring","Only after the establishment of a single information system, i.e. electronic register for criminal offences with a corrupt element, precise systematization and classification of data will be established, as well as regular verification and exchange of information, which will enable reliable reporting on corruption and organized crime.",""],[1,"18","1","Compatible Case Monitoring Forms for Justice Institutions","Mutually compatible forms in the police, courts and prosecutor's offices should also include the possibility of monitoring cases of proactive actions, acting upon reports of the Agency, State Audit Institution, Tax Administration, Public Procurement Administration, etc.",""],[1,"18","2","Organized Crime Investigation and Asset Recovery Measures","Also, in the field of fight against organized crime, the Republic of Serbia should show convincing results in terms of effec- tive investigations, prosecutions and final judgements in organized crime cases, including finan- cial investigations; it should systematically strengthen the freezing and confiscation of proceeds from crime and ensure clear separation of powers and regulations regarding the interception of communications for criminal investigations and for security purposes.",""],[1,"19","1","International Asset Confiscation for Corruption Proceeds","Confiscation of the property acquired through corruption on the international level is the most important aspect of this Convention.",""],[1,"24","1","National Strategy for the Fight Against Organised Crime","National Strategy for the Fight Against Organised Crime (not-time bound, accom- panying AP has expired)",""],[1,"24","1","National Strategy for the Prevention and Fight Against Terrorism","National Strategy for the Prevention and Fight Against the Terrorism for the period from 2016 to 2021 (with the accompanying AP)",""],[1,"24","1","Cybercrime Prevention and Suppression Strategy","Strategy for the Fight Against Cybercrime for the period from 2019 to 2023 (accompanying AP has expired)",""],[1,"21","3","National Strategy for the Fight Against Organized Crime","A direct connection with the same target 16.4. is also established in the National Strategy for the Fight Against Organized Crime (not- time bound, accompanying AP has expired) which envisages general measures of institution building and capacity building for the fight against organized crime.",""],[1,"21","3","Chapter 24 Action Plan on Organized Crime and Money Laundering","The Action Plan for Negotiating Chapter 24 deals extensively with issues of organized crime and money laundering, and the whole special subchapter is dedicated to this issue.",""],[1,"21","3","Criminal Intelligence and Financial Investigation Measures","It envisions activities to introduce a criminal intelligence system, link prosecuting authorities, conduct complex financial investigations, increase the seizure of proceeds of crime and strengthen firearms control.",""]],"38":[[1,"16","4","Amendment of the Law on Non-Contentious Proceedings for Birth Registration","by amending the Law on Non-Contentious Proceedings it is possible to subsequently register in the birth register, which is important for the Roma population.",""],[1,"16","4","Electronic Birth Certificate Register and Online Birth Registration","Keeping a register of birth certificates in electronic form and the possibility of registering the birth of a child electronically contribute to achieving this goal.",""],[1,"23","3","Birth Registration and Legal Identity Measures for Roma","the exercise of the right of members of the Roma national minority to registration in the register of births in administrative procedure has been ensured, as well as effective judicial protection in the procedure of determining time and place of birth .",""]],"39":[[1,"16","5","Establishment of Independent Regulatory Bodies","Independent regulatory bodies have been established",""],[1,"17","3","Anti-Corruption Law and Agency Strengthening","The Action Plan for Chapter 23 envisages that the key measure for the prevention of corruption is the adoption of the new Law on Prevention of Corruption, which was adopted by the National Assembly on 31 May 2019.",""],[1,"18","2","Anti-Corruption Coordination and Enforcement Mechanism","In its fight against corruption, the Republic of Serbia should build an effective coordination mechanism that would operationalise the objectives of prevention policy and effectively deal with corruption, improve records of inves- tigations, indictments and final judgements in high-level corrupt-related cases, including confis- cation of proceeds from crime, effectively implement all pieces of anti-corruption legislation in order to strengthen the role of the Anti-Corruption Agency and adopt a new anti-corruption strat- egy.",""],[1,"21","4","National Anti-Corruption Strategy","This Strategy was the basic national policy document in this area.",""],[1,"21","4","Law on Prevention of Corruption","Currently, this area is mostly covered by the Law on Prevention of Corruption the Law on Lobbying .",""],[1,"21","4","Law on Lobbying","Currently, this area is mostly covered by the Law on Prevention of Corruption the Law on Lobbying .",""]],"40":[[1,"17","3","Public Sector Transparency and Inclusiveness Reforms","substantial reforms of the public sector are being carried out in the direction of greater transparency and inclusiveness.",""],[1,"22","2","Public Administration Reform Strategy","The target 16.6 effective and transparent institutions is the central topic of the Public Administration Reform Strategy of the Republic of Serbia for the period from 2021 to 2030 and the accompanying AP for the period from 2021 to 2025, being the umbrella public policy document that is to ensure the continuation of the previous reforms and their extension to the entire public sector, and not only to the public administration.",""],[1,"22","4","Civil Servant Professional Development Programmes","Other instruments of support to the Public Administration Reform Strategy in the Republic of Serbia are the Professional Development Programmes of Civil Servants in the Republic of Serbia and the Professional Development Programme of Employees in Local Government Units, which aim to contribute to increasing the efficiency and economy of public administration and its effectiveness in exercising rights and the interests of citizens, economic entities and other holders of rights and obligations, through the creation of conditions for continuous and compre- hensive increase in the level of competencies of civil servants, which directly affects target 16.6.",""],[1,"23","1","Public Policy Consultation and Evidence-Based Decision-Making Reform","public policies are to be adopted on the basis of previously con- ducted analyses and be based on facts",""],[1,"23","1","Public Policy Management and Regulatory Reform Programme","Programme for Improving Public Pol- icy Management and Regulatory Reform for the Period from 2021 to 2025 (in the adoption procedure) will contribute to the improvement of the consultative process",""],[1,"33","3","Preparation of Policy Impact Assessment Guidelines","guidelines according to the EU methodology have been prepared for such assessments.",""],[1,"47","7","Economic Reform Programme Structural Reform Monitoring","The Economic Reform Programme prioritizes structural reforms that are already contained in sectoral strategies and enables centralized monitoring of their implementation, but also measuring their social impact and impact on competitiveness.",""]],"41":[[1,"17","3","Corruption and Organized Crime Prosecution Capacity","a key measure of the Action Plan for Chapter 23 is the development of efficient and proactive action in detecting and prosecuting corruption and organized crime.",""]],"42":[[1,"18","2","Human Rights and Anti-Discrimination Strategy Package","With regard to fundamental rights, the Republic of Serbia should strengthen human rights institutions and guarantee their independence, adopt and implement new anti-discrimination strategies, actively investigate and convict hate crimes, and ensure consistent implementation of national legislation relating to minorities, including the Roma population.",""],[1,"19","9","Strategy for the Rights of Persons with Disabilities 2021-2030","Strategy for the Rights of Persons with Disabilities for the period from 2021 to 2030 contributes to strengthening social inclusion and implementation of non-discriminatory policies at the EU level.",""],[1,"24","2","New Strategy for Prevention of Discrimination","A new Strategy is being drafted.",""],[1,"38","3","New Strategy for Prevention and Protection against Discrimination","the preparation of a new Strategy for Prevention and Protection against Discrimination is under- way",""],[1,"44","1","Accessibility of Facilities, Public Areas, Information, Services and Products for Persons with Disabilities","One of the measures of this Strategy is to ensure full accessibility of facilities, public areas, information, services and products to persons with disabil- ities, in order to make the entire environment equally accessible to persons with disabilities.",""],[1,"23","2","Priority Employment Regulations for Underrepresented Minorities","the Government has adopted regulations based on the Law on Employees in Autonomous Provinces and Local Self-Government Units, which give priority to the employment of members of underrepresented minorities.",""]],"43":[[1,"19","1","Witness and Whistleblower Protection Measures","The protection of witnesses and whistleblowers is also envisaged.",""],[1,"20","1","Police Community Strategy","Police Community Strategy (is not time-bound, but its AP has expired) deals with the introduction of policing models based on the close connections with local communities and the joint action by the police and communities to tackle security issues.",""]],"44":[[1,"20","3","Action Plan for Prevention, Protection and Support Against Violence Against Children","the Action Plan for the period from 2020 and 2021 represents a comprehensive response of society to violence against children, in accordance with the dynamics of challenges, risks and threats, through an improved prevention, protection and support system.",""],[1,"20","3","Child Rights and Juvenile Justice Improvement Measures","The Action Plan for Chapter 23 envisages a number of measures to improve the rights of the child (improvement of juvenile justice in order to fully implement European standards).",""],[1,"20","4","Domestic Violence Prevention Law Implementation","Law on Prevention of Domestic Violence was adopted on 23 November 2016.",""],[1,"20","4","Specialist Training for Justice and Police Officials","Specialist training of judges, prosecutors and police officials is being continuously implemented, in order to efficiently apply new statutory solutions and de- crease the number of children suffering violence in the hands of their carers",""],[1,"24","1","Child Violence Prevention and Protection Strategy","Strategy for Pre- vention and Protection of Children from Violence (with the accompanying AP for 2020 and 2021)",""]],"45":[[1,"19","8","Anti-Trafficking Convention Implementation","Council of Europe Convention on Action against Trafficking adopted in 2005, prohibits all forms of trafficking in human beings, simultaneously dedicating particular attention to the protection of human trafficking victims.",""],[1,"20","5","Strategy for Prevention and Suppression of Trafficking in Human Beings","Strategy of Prevention and Suppression of Trafficking in Human Beings, Especially Women and Children and Protection of Victims for the period from 2017 to 2022 (accompanying AP has expired) is also related to the target 16.2, especially the UN indicator 16.2.2 (number of human trafficking victims).",""],[1,"20","5","Measures to Prevent and Sanction Human Trafficking","This document envisages a series of measures aimed at preventing and sanc- tioning trafficking in human beings, with an emphasis on the protection of children from human trafficking and exploitation in pornography and prostitution and their consequences.",""],[1,"20","5","Action Plan for Chapter 24 Capacity-Building Measures","The Action Plan for Chapter 24 envisages a series of measures which Serbia is obliged to implement in order to build up its capacities to combat trafficking in human beings.",""],[1,"49","5","Strategy for the Prevention and Suppression of Trafficking in Human Beings","This Strategy has contributed to the fight against trafficking in human beings through the creation of conditions for the improvement of the system of prevention, assistance and protection of victims.",""],[1,"46","1","Eradication of Human Trafficking, Forced Labour, and Child Labour","It is necessary to eradicate human trafficking and forced labour, especially child labour (8.7).",""]],"46":[[1,"21","2","Small Arms and Light Weapons Control Strategy","Small Arms and Light Weapons Control Strategy for the period from 2019 to 2024 (accom- panying AP has expired) aims to reduce the threat of illegal possession and misuse of small arms and light weapons, ammunition and explosives for civilian use.",""],[1,"21","2","Weapons of Mass Destruction Proliferation Prevention Strategy","Strategy for Combating the Proliferation of Weapons of Mass Destruction for the period from 2021 to 2025 (without accompanying AP) contributes towards increasing the level of security and safety.",""]],"47":[[1,"22","2","E-Government Development and Anti-Corruption Measures","This Strategy envisages the development of e-government, as well as more activities to combat corruption.",""],[1,"22","3","E-Government Development Programme","The e-Government Development Programme of the Republic of Serbia for the period 2020 to 2022 with its accompanying Action plan provides for the technical support to the Public Administration Reform Strategy of the Republic of Serbia and is closely related to it.",""],[1,"22","3","E-Government Infrastructure and Interoperability Development","The following specific objectives have been defined: development of infrastructure in e-government and ensuring interoperability, improving legal certainty in the use of e-government, increasing the availability of e-government to citizens and the economy through improving customer service and opening data in public administration.",""],[1,"22","3","Public Administration Database Connectivity and e-ZUP Services","According to the report on the implementation of the APIGP, the connection of the 6 state bodies' databases has been completed: Registers (RB, RM, RD), Mol - residence and Mol - biometric documents, PA - inquiry, NEA - review of records and certificate of paid amounts, CROSO - verification of employment status, PDIF - records of beneficiaries). Access to connected databases is provided through the e-ZUP services, which started operating on June 2020.",""]],"48":[[1,"23","4","Public Information System Development Strategy","Strategy for the Development of the Public Information System of the Republic of Serbia for the period from 2020 to 2025 with the accompanying AP for the period from 2020 to 2022 constitutes a legal framework to exercise: freedom of expression, freedom of the media, security of journalists, me- dia pluralism, developed media market, strengthened journalistic profession, educated citizens and institutions capable of enforcing regulations.",""],[1,"23","4","Personal Data Protection Strategy","The Strategy for the Protection of Personal Data (working group has been formed) will additionally contribute to the regulation of the protection of fundamental rights and freedoms.",""]],"49":[[1,"26","2","Organized Cancer Screening Programmes","the Republic of Serbia has been doing since the introduction of organized screening programmes since 2012.",""],[1,"26","2","Breast Cancer Mammography Screening Programme","The Republic of Serbia has started a programme for early detection of breast cancer, mam- mography screening, which is free for all women aged 50 to 69.",""],[1,"26","2","Cervical Cancer Early Detection Screening Programme","an organized screening programme for early detection of cervical cancer has been launched, which is free for all women aged 25 to 64.",""],[1,"30","5","Cancer Screening Improvement Programme","Programme for Improving Cancer Screening in the Republic of Serbia for 2020-2022 along with its Action Plan was adopted with the view to establishing better cancer control through better planning and coordination of a wide range of services provided within the national and health-care system, from prevention and health improvement to rehabilitation and palliative care.",""]],"50":[[1,"26","3","Early Warning System for New Psychoactive Substances","With the support of the European Monitoring Centre for Drugs and Drug Addiction - EMCDDA, an early warning system for new psychoactive substances has been established within the Centre for Monitoring Drugs and Drug Addiction.",""],[1,"26","3","Protocol on the Early Warning System for New Psychoactive Substances","The Protocol on the Early Warning System for New Psychoactive Substances has also been completed.",""],[1,"26","3","Legal Framework for Psychoactive Controlled Substances","The international cooperation of the Ministry of Health in this area is defined by the Law on Psychoactive Controlled Substances.","Ministry of Health"],[1,"30","7","New Drug Abuse Prevention Strategy","The plan is to develop a new strategy that would be valid from 2022.",""],[1,"30","7","National Programme for Prevention of Harmful Alcohol Use","Likewise, National Programme for the Prevention of Harmful Use of Alcohol and Alcohol-Induced Disorders was adopted in 2017, it is not time-bound and has no accompanying AP.",""]],"51":[[1,"27","3","Comprehensive Tobacco Control Law Harmonization","the focus must be on harmonizing the Law on Tobacco with Directive 2014/40/EU, i.e. on drafting a comprehensive law on tobacco control and amendments to the Law on Tobacco, in order to apply the highest standards in the field of safety and health.",""],[1,"28","8","Tobacco Control Measures under the WHO Framework Convention","Serbia is obliged to apply different measures for tobacco control that will reduce offer and demand for tobacco products, and thus the harmful effects on citizens health.",""],[1,"31","5","Implementation of Tobacco Control Measures under the Public Health Strategy","the implementation of the World Health Organization Framework Convention on Tobacco Control will be attained through the implementation of measures envisaged under the Public Health Strategy of the Republic of Serbia for the period 2018 to 2026 with its accompanying Action Plan.",""]],"52":[[1,"28","4","Women's Reproductive Health and Family Planning Access Measures","states have to ensure equal access to medical services, including measures for families planning and free medical attention and appropriate nutrition during pregnancy, post-natal period and breast-feed- ing.",""],[1,"36","6","National Programme for Preservation and Improvement of Sexual and Reproductive Health","Making independent decisions on sexual and reproductive health based on relevant information, respect, protection, fulfilment and guarantee of sexual and reproductive rights is integrated at the level of specific objectives in the National Programme for Preservation and Improvement of Sexual and Reproductive Health of Citizens of the Republic of Serbia (not time-bound, no accompanying AP).",""],[1,"37","5","National Sexual and Reproductive Health Programme","National Programme for Preservation and Improvement of Sexual and Reproductive Health of Citizens of the Republic of Serbia (not time-bound, no accompanying AP)",""],[1,"31","2","Birth Incentive Strategy","the Birth Incentive Strategy was adopted (not time- bound, without accompanying AP), which, as a special goal, among other things, states the mitigation of the economic cost of raising a child; reconciling work and parenthood; strengthening the psychological cost of parenthood; promoting reproductive health and combating infertility.",""],[1,"31","3","National Breastfeeding and Newborn Developmental Care Programme","the National Programme for Support of Breastfeeding, Family and Developmental Care of Newborns which was adopted in 2018 (not time-bound, no accompanying AP), endeavours to help families in the right approach to raising children at a more sensitive age.",""]],"53":[[1,"28","5","Mental Health Rights and Care Standards Framework","Resolution on Principles on Protection of Persons with Mental Illness (1991) and for Improve- ment of Mental Health Care promotes the rights of persons with mental illness and includes prop- ositions related to informed agreement, secrecy of data and standards for medical care and treat- ment.",""],[1,"30","3","National Mental Health Protection Programme","The National Programme for the Protection of Mental Health in the Republic of Serbia for the period 2019-2026 with the accompanying Action Plan until 2022 contributes to the same target",""]],"54":[[1,"28","7","Health Policy Participation and Equity Commitment","By Tallinn Charter \"Health System for Health and Wealth\" member countries are committed, among other, to promote joint values for solidarity, equity and participation in creation of health policies, planning and distribution of resources and other activities that provide for paying special attention to the needs of poor and other sensitive population groups;",""],[1,"28","7","Health System Investment Promotion","to invest in health systems and stimulate investments in other sectors;",""],[1,"28","7","Health System Transparency and Accountability","to promote transparency and to be responsible for the results of health systems so as to attain measurable results.",""],[1,"29","4","Public Health Acquis Compliance Programme","Serbia continues to comply with European standards in public health areas, such as: biomedicine, tobacco control, cancer screening, infectious diseases, alcohol and drugs, nutrition, health inequalities, rare diseases, cross-border healthcare provision, pharmaceuticals and cosmetics.",""],[1,"29","5","Public Health Strategy and Action Plan 2018-2026","Current Public Health Strategy of the Republic of Serbia for the period from 2018 to 2026 with its accompanying Action Plan for the period from 2018 to 2026, is at present the most comprehensive document in the field of preservation and improvement of health and health care.",""]],"55":[[1,"30","1","Health Care Development Strategy 2026","the development of a new strategy for the development of health care in the Republic of Serbia for the period until 2026 has begun.",""],[1,"30","1","Health Planning Framework Optimization","the optimization of the planning frame- work should regulate the hierarchical relationship of the documents and reduce the number of programmes that determine public policies for communicable and chronic non-communicable diseases, as well as integrate policies established in programmes that do not have a term.",""]],"56":[[1,"30","4","Programme for Rare Disease","Programme for Rare Disease of the Republic of Serbia for the period from 2020 to 2022, with the accompanying Action Plan was adopted.",""]],"57":[[1,"35","2","National Disaster Risk Management Programme","National Disaster Risk Management Programme (not time-bound, without accompanying AP) is the most important strategic document directly linked with the target 1.5.",""],[1,"60","4","National Disaster Risk Management Programme","National Disaster Risk Management Programme (not time-bound, accompanying AP has ex- pired) provides support to the Government's efforts to align with the EU acquis, in particular the Water Management Directive, the Floods Directive, and the Climate Change Adaptation Direc- tive., as well as the Civil Society Directive.",""],[1,"60","4","National Strategy for Protection and Rescue in Emergency Situations","National Strategy for Protection and Rescue in Emergency Situations (not time-bound and no accompanying AP) through strategic areas of planning and risk management seeks to contribute to the reduction of economic and human losses caused by natural disasters.",""],[1,"67","4","National Disaster Risk Management Programme","National Disaster Risk Management Programme (not time-bound, without accompanying AP) should be stressed.",""],[1,"67","4","Disaster Risk Financing Programme of the Republic of Serbia","Disaster Risk Financing Programme of the Republic of Serbia was valid until 2019.",""],[1,"67","5","National Disaster Risk Reduction and Rescue Strategy","National Strategy for Protection and Rescue in the State of Emergency (not time-bound, no accompanying AP) is implemented through strategic areas in line with the Hyogo Framework for Action: making disaster risk reduction a national and a local priority with a strong institutional basis for implementation; identify, assess and monitor disaster risks and enhance early warning; use knowledge, innovation and education to build a culture of safety and resilience at all levels; reduce the underlying risk factors; and strengthen disaster preparedness for effective response at all levels.",""]],"58":[[1,"34","4","Employment Strategy and Action Plan 2021-2026","The Employment Strategy of the Republic of Serbia for the period from 2021 to 2026 with the accompanying Action Plan for the period from 2021 to 2023 is of great importance for the attainment of these goals.",""],[1,"36","4","Measures to Improve Women's Position in the Labour Market","Measures for improving the position of women in the labour market are specifically defined under the mentioned goal.",""],[1,"49","3","Employment Strategy 2021-2026 and Action Plan","A large number of activities aimed at achieving the target 8.5 achieve full and productive em- ployment and decent work for all women and men, including for young people and persons with disabilities, and equal pay for work of equal value is defined under the Employment Strategy of the Republic of Serbia for the period from 2021 to 2026 and the accompanying AP for the period from 2021 to 2023.",""],[1,"49","3","Inter-Sectoral Cooperation and Employment Institution Strengthening","The priorities of this Strategy are to increase the level of inter- sectoral cooperation, improve the position of the unemployed and strengthen the institutional framework.",""],[1,"49","3","Women's Labour Market Inclusion Measures","The Strategy also defines systemic preconditions for improving the position of women in the labour market by encouraging women's entrepreneurship, exercising rights from the in- surance system in low-skilled jobs, inclusion in additional education and training, granting subsi- dies for self-employment, applying the principle of gender responsive budgeting and integrating women from underdeveloped and devastated areas.",""],[1,"49","4","National Youth Employability and Employment Strategy","Target 8.6 substantially reduce the proportion of youth not in employment, education or train- ing is one of the main priorities of the National Youth Strategy for the period from 2015 to 2025 (accompanying AP has expired).",""],[1,"49","4","Youth Labour Market Integration Strategy","The improved position of young people on the labour mar- ket is an integral part of the Employment Strategy of the Republic of Serbia for the period from 2021 to 2026 and the accompanying AP for the period from 2021 to 2023.",""]],"59":[[1,"39","3","Migration Management Strategy","The umbrella strategy in this area is the Mi- gration Management Strategy (accompanying AP has expired).",""]],"60":[[1,"34","5","Education Accessibility and Inclusion Measures","The Action Plan defines measures to solve this problem by improving the accessibility, fairness, comprehensiveness and openness of pre-university and higher education.",""],[1,"42","8","Inclusive Education Action Plan","The Action Plan includes activities related to inclusive education: development of special curricula, training of teaching staff, educational cam- paigns, establishment of resource centres and development of a roadmap and optimal model of intersecotral funding.",""],[1,"43","1","Roma Education Inclusion Strategy","the priority is to ensure full inclusion of children and youth from the Roma community in quality pre-school, primary and secondary education, greater coverage of Roma men and women in the student population and support for the education of young people and adults who have not attended or have dropped out of school, with the introduction of effective and efficient mechanisms to combat discrimination and enjoy all minority conditions rights for Roma men and women in the education system.",""],[1,"43","2","Affirmative Enrollment Measures in Higher Education","Affirmative measures for enrolment in faculties still exist in the form of place norms that are kept for certain groups of students in each programme.",""],[1,"43","3","Roma Early School Dropout Prevention Mechanisms","One of the priorities of the above-mentioned Strategy for Social Inclusion of Roma of the Republic of Serbia for the period from 2016 to 2025 is to provide effective and efficient mechanisms for prevention of early school dropout (especially girls) from the Roma community at the transition from the fourth to the fifth grade and at the transition from primary to secondary education, as well as the capacities of educational institutions for their implementation.",""],[1,"37","5","Education Strategy for Equal Access for Boys and Girls","Strategy for the Development of Education by 2030 (AP for the period 2021 to 2023) that integrates the principle of equal access to education for boys and girls.",""]],"61":[[1,"43","4","Environmental Education and Sustainable Development Training Activities","The Action Plan defines activities for the attainment of this goal (accreditation of trainings related to sustainable development, training of teaching staff on sustainable development, development and implementation of trainings to strengthen students' capacity to carry out activities related to sustainable development, collective well-being and democratic culture).",""],[1,"43","4","Elective Education for Sustainable Development Programme","During the academic year 2019/20 high school students of I and II grade had the op- portunity to study the elective programme Education for Sustainable Development.",""],[1,"43","4","New Elective Programmes for Upper Secondary Education","In the next two academic years, within the offer for III and IV grade, with two hours a week, a number of new elective programmes will be introduced into the educational practice, including Education for Sustainable Development .",""],[1,"64","3","Sustainable Development Education Curriculum Integration","Strategy for the Development of Education in the Republic of Serbia until 2030 and the accompanying AP for the period from 2021 to 2023 continues to include topics of sustainable development in the curricula",""],[1,"64","3","Sustainable Development Training Accreditation","Some of the activities for the realization of this goal are: accreditation of trainings related to sustainable development",""],[1,"64","3","Teacher Training on Sustainable Development","training of teaching staff on sustainable development",""],[1,"64","3","Student Capacity-Building for Sustainable Development Activities","development and implementation of trainings to strengthen students' capacity to carry out activities related to sustainable development, collective well-being and democratic culture",""]],"62":[[1,"43","5","School Violence Prevention and Educational Function Strengthening","Strengthening the educational function of schools at all levels of education with the aim of pre- venting violence is a priority in the Education Strategy, which is important for the attainment of 4.a to build and improve educational facilities (adapted to people with disabilities, safe, non-violent, inclusive and effective learning environments).",""],[1,"43","5","Educational Infrastructure Improvement","Strategy for the Development of Education also recognizes the importance of improving the educational infrastructure for the quality of education and the physical accessibility of the space in which the educational process takes place.",""]],"63":[[1,"46","6","Investment Plan for Europe","The Investment Plan for Europe plans to, in the period from 2021 to 2027 , mobilizes more than 372 billion euros for investments in four key areas: sustainable infrastructure (energy, transport, water, environment, culture, digital infrastructure), research, innovation and digitalisa- tion (innovation and business process research, technology transfer and business digitisation), small and medium-sized enterprises (access to finance and additional support for small and me- dium-sized enterprises) medium-sized enterprises) and social protection and skills (microfinance, social entrepreneurship, education, gender equality, health, inclusion).",""],[1,"46","6","Horizon Research and Innovation Framework Programme","European framework for science and innovation \"Horizon\" for the period from 2021 to 2027 is largely focused on greater competitiveness of the European economy through the development and application of new technologies.",""],[1,"47","2","Regulatory Harmonization and EU Programme Participation","In addition to harmonizing regulations, the Republic of Serbia, as a candidate country for EU membership, participates in three European Union programmes that are extremely important for topics covered by SDG 8.",""],[1,"52","2","Investment Plan for Europe","The Investment Plan for Eu- rope, described in SDG 8, covers strategic investments in the areas of infrastructure, science, in- novation and financial instruments to support innovative companies.",""],[1,"52","3","Participation in Horizon 2021-2027 Science and Innovation Framework","The European Framework for Science and Innovation \"Horizon 2021-2027\", in which the Republic of Serbia has the right to participate on an equal footing with member states, generates significant investments in science and new technologies and largely focuses scientific research on developing new technologies and solving major societal challenges.",""]],"64":[[1,"48","2","Smart Specialisation Strategy and Action Plan","The strategic framework for improving the general technological level of industry in Serbia has been further improved within the Smart Specialisation Strategy in the Republic of Serbia for the period from 2020 to 2027 with the accompanying Action Plan for the period from 2021 to 2022",""],[1,"48","2","Industrial Policy Strategy and Action Plan","the Industrial Policy Strategy of the Republic of Serbia from 2021 to 2030 with the accompanying Action Plan for the period from 2021 to 2023",""],[1,"54","4","Smart Specialisation Strategy and Action Plan","Smart Specialisation Strategy of the Republic of Serbia for the period from 2020 to 2027 with the accompanying Action Plan for the period from 2021 to 2022 defines the general objective: Directed development of the Republic of Serbia towards a highly competitive economy through research, development, innovation and entrepreneurial initiatives in the areas of 4S.",""],[1,"54","4","Joint Research and Development Projects","One of the important goals in the field of machines and production processes of the future is to improve the cooperation of companies with scientific research organizations by initiating joint research and development projects.",""]],"65":[[1,"49","2","Industrial Policy Strategy for 2021-2030 with Action Plan","Industrial Policy Strategy of the Republic of Serbia for the period from 2021 to 2030 and the accompanying AP for the period from 2021 to 2023, within the circular economy as one of the strategic areas of intervention within which goals and measures are defined, includes environmental protection",""],[1,"49","2","Waste Management Programme","The Waste Management Programme and the Cleaner Production Programme (which are under development) will create better conditions for environmental conservation.",""],[1,"49","2","Cleaner Production Programme","The Waste Management Programme and the Cleaner Production Programme (which are under development) will create better conditions for environmental conservation.",""],[1,"51","5","Industrial Infrastructure Upgrade and Retrofit Programme","To attain the target 9.4 upgrade infrastructure and retrofit industries to make them sustain- able, with increased resource-use efficiency and greater adoption of clean and sound technolo- gies",""],[1,"64","4","Cleaner Production Programme","The Cleaner Production Programme, Circular Economy Programme and the Waste Management Programme, which are under preparation, will contribute to the progress of the conditions under 12.2, 12.3, 12.4 and 12.5.",""],[1,"64","4","Circular Economy Programme","The Cleaner Production Programme, Circular Economy Programme and the Waste Management Programme, which are under preparation, will contribute to the progress of the conditions under 12.2, 12.3, 12.4 and 12.5.",""],[1,"64","4","Waste Management Programme","The Cleaner Production Programme, Circular Economy Programme and the Waste Management Programme, which are under preparation, will contribute to the progress of the conditions under 12.2, 12.3, 12.4 and 12.5.",""],[1,"68","9","Cleaner Production Programme","Cleaner Production Programme (under development) will contribute towards archiving SDG 13.2 through more rational and environmental-friendly use of resources in the production processes.",""]],"66":[[1,"49","6","Employment Strategy and Occupational Safety and Health Strategy","This topic is covered under the Employment Strategy of the Republic of Serbia for the period from 2021 to 2026 and the accompanying AP for the period from 2021 to 2023 and Occupational Safety and Health Strategy of the Republic of Serbia for the period from 2018 to 2022 and the accompanying AP for the period from 2018 to 2022.",""],[1,"50","1","Occupational Safety and Health Regulatory Harmonization and Awareness Programme","represents a continuous work on improving the field of occupational safety and health through, further harmonization of regulations with EU regulations, as well as through joint work of employers, employees, trade unions and the state to improve and raise awareness in this area, improving skills, i.e. establishing a culture of work and creating preconditions for well-being at work and quality of life and health at work.",""]],"67":[[1,"50","2","Tourism Development Strategy for Sustainable Tourism","The first objective of the Tourism Development Strategy of the Republic of Serbia for the period from 2016 to 2025 with the accompanying AP for the period from 2016 to 2025 is sustainable economic, ecological and social development of the tourism in the Republic of Serbia.",""]],"68":[[1,"56","3","Urban Wastewater Treatment Directive Implementation","The Framework Directive includes and links other directives directly or indirectly related to the area of water, two of which are the most important: The Urban Wastewater Treatment Directive and the Directive on the Quality of Water Intended for Human Consumption, i.e. the Drinking Water Directive.",""],[1,"56","3","Drinking Water Directive Implementation","The Framework Directive includes and links other directives directly or indirectly related to the area of water, two of which are the most important: The Urban Wastewater Treatment Directive and the Directive on the Quality of Water Intended for Human Consumption, i.e. the Drinking Water Directive.",""],[1,"56","5","Drinking Water Directive Transposition","SDG 6 is implemented in Serbia through the transposition of two key EU directives.",""],[1,"56","5","Urban Wastewater Treatment Directive Implementation","The investment needs for the implementation of the Drinking Water Directive, and in particular the Urban Wastewater Treatment Directive, are enormous.",""]],"69":[[1,"53","4","Mineral Resources Management Strategy","The Mineral Resources Management Strategy of the Republic of Serbia until 2030 additionally contributes to the improvement of the situation in the field of energy and sustainable use of natural resources.",""],[1,"54","2","National Strategy for Sustainable Use of Natural Resources and Assets","National Strategy for Sustainable Use of Natural Resources and Assets (not time-bound and no accompanying AP) (not time-bound and no accompanying AP), which defines an environmen- tally friendly link between natural resources and goods as inputs in the production process and industrial activities in which these resources are used, contributes to this goal.",""]],"70":[[1,"58","1","Coordinated Energy Development Framework","SDG 7 is implemented in Serbia through a set of strategic documents and institutional arrange- ments that ensure coordinated energy development of the region of Southeast Europe.",""],[1,"58","1","Energy and Environmental Acquis Implementation","The Energy acquis and the part of the environmental acquis, through which the highest European stan- dards in this area are pursued, are implemented under the supervision of the Energy Community for South East Europe.",""],[1,"58","6","Regional Energy Infrastructure Expansion","Expand energy infrastructure (7.b.) at the regional level is supported through a list of priority projects of the Energy Community, which meet the general and specific criteria for Trans-Europe- an Energy Infrastructure (PECI) and whose long-term benefits outweigh the costs and cross-bor- der dimension.",""],[1,"58","6","Energy Sector Cooperation and Capacity Strengthening","Through the Energy Strategy, the Energy Community of South East Europe encourages the strengthening of the energy sector through international cooperation (UN indicator 7.a.1) and the improvement of infrastructure and technological capacities (UN indicator 7.b.1).",""]],"71":[[1,"59","1","Urban and Settlement Development Policy Reform","Therefore, there is a need to introduce modern, contemporary principles of sustainable urban development in line with EU policies and the UN Urban Agenda.",""],[1,"59","3","Strategy for Sustainable Urban Development","Target 11.3 inclusive and sustainable urbanisation is the topic covered by the Strategy for Sustainable Urban De- velopment of the Republic of Serbia until 2030 with the Action Plan for the period from 2021 to 2022.",""],[1,"60","1","Implementation of the New Urban Agenda through Participatory Urban Policies","Member States have committed themselves to transposing the New Urban Agenda through implementing and participatory urban policies at national and subnational level",""],[1,"60","2","Strategy for Sustainable Urban Development","By adopting the Strategy for Sustainable Urban Development, the Republic of Serbia has transferred the New Urban Agenda of the United Nations to the national level, within its national framework.",""],[1,"60","2","New Spatial Plan Development","Also, it is the basis for the development of a new Spatial Plan of the Republic of Serbia.",""],[1,"60","3","Adoption of the New Spatial Plan of the Republic of Serbia","it is important to adopt a new Spatial Plan of the Republic of Serbia (public debate finalised)",""],[1,"61","2","Sustainable Urban Development Strategy and Action Plan","Sustainable Urban Development Strategy of the Republic of Serbia until 2030 with its accom- panying AP for the period 2021 to 2022 contributes towards achieving target 11.7 provide univer- sal access to safe, inclusive and accessible green and public spaces.",""],[1,"61","3","Sustainable Urban Development Strategy and Action Plan","Strengthening national and regional development planning (11.a) is contained in the Sustainable Urban Development Strategy of the Republic of Serbia until 2030 with the Action Plan for the period from 2021 to 2022.",""],[1,"61","4","Integrated Urban Policies and Plans for Inclusion, Resource Efficiency, and Disaster Risk Reduction","The implementation of integrated policies and plans aimed at inclusion, resource efficiency and disaster risk reduction in accordance with the Snedai Framework at the level of cities and settlements (11.b) is an integral part of the Sustainable Urban Development Strategy of Serbia until 2030 with accompanying Action Plan for the period from 2021 to 2022.",""]],"72":[[1,"34","5","Roma Housing Tenure and Women's Ownership Inclusion","The topic of regulating the ownership and legal status of housing in Roma settlements and increasing the participation of Roma women in ownership is recognized within the Strategy for Social Inclusion of Roma in the Republic of Serbia for the period from 2016",""],[1,"59","2","National Social Housing Strategy and Action Plan","SDG 11, and in particular target 11.1. regarding the access for all to adequate, safe and afford- able housing and basic services, is implemented through the policies formulated under the National Social Housing Strategy and its accompanying Action Plan until 2022.",""],[1,"59","2","Strategy for Social Inclusion of Roma","Strategy for Social Inclusion of Roma of the Republic of Serbia in the period from 2016 to 2025 (accompanying AP has expired), which aims to improve the living conditions of Roma in accordance with international standards regarding the right to adequate housing, also contrib- utes to improving housing conditions.",""],[1,"59","2","National Housing Strategy Drafting","The National Housing Strategy is being drafted .",""]],"73":[[1,"64","2","Public Procurement Sustainability and Innovation Programme","The key goal is to promote and encourage environmental and social aspects in public procurement and innovations.",""]],"74":[[1,"54","2","National Emission Reduction Plan","Republic of Serbia's National Emission Reduction Plan, adopted by the Government in June 2015, whereby Serbia committed to reducing emission levels by 9.8% relative to the 1990 level, by 2030, plays also significant role in the achieving the target 9.4 retrofit industries to make them sustainable, with increased resource-use efficiency and and environmentally sound tech- nologies.",""],[1,"54","2","Climate Change Law and Emissions Monitoring System","The Law on Climate Change has been adopted, and it should regulate the system for limiting greenhouse gas emissions, the system for adapting to changed climatic conditions, as well as the system for monitoring, reporting and verification.",""],[1,"65","3","Integration of Climate Change Measures into National Policies and Planning","It is necessary to integrate climate change measures into national policies, strategies and planning (13.2).",""],[1,"65","4","Climate Change Monitoring, Reporting and Verification System","the Republic of Serbia has started establishing a system for monitoring, reporting and verification (MRV), which is one of the main requirements of the UN Framework Convention on Climate Change and is in line with the Paris Agreement.",""],[1,"65","5","Environmental Protection and Climate Change Mitigation Directives","the EU has adopted a series of directives setting the highest stan- dards in fostering sustainable development.",""],[1,"66","4","Climate Action Group Cooperation Platform","In mid-2017, Climate Action Group was set up within the Energy Community of South East Europe acting as a platform for cooperation between representatives of ministries and other relevant institutions in charge of energy, climate change and environment.",""],[1,"66","4","Climate Policy Development and Legal Transposition Support","The goal of the initiative is to support both the development of climate policy and transposition of the relevant regulation into national legislations, and effective implementation of the policy and setting of new 2030 target goals for the signatories.",""],[1,"66","4","Sustainability Forum for Sustainable Energy Transition","The Energy Community and the Balkan Green Foundation have set up the so-called Sustainability Forum which brings together a number of stakeholders, focusing on transition towards sustainable energy.",""],[1,"66","4","Western Balkans Sustainable Energy and Climate Cooperation MoU","In parallel, a Memorandum of Understanding was signed with the EBRD with a view to strengthening cooperation in the area of sustainable energy devel- opment and climate change in the Western Balkans.",""],[1,"66","6","Nationally Determined Contributions and Paris Agreement Reporting","Key provisions of the 2015 Paris Agreement foresee the following: holding the increase in the global average temperature to well below 2℃ above pre-industrial levels; adoption of nationally determined contributions, i.e. target goals, and revision thereof every five years as well as development of measures with the aim of achieving the objectives of contributions; regular reporting on emissions and the progress made in regard to national target goals.",""],[1,"66","8","EU Climate Action Initiative","the EU launched the Climate Action, with the aim of making Europe neutral on GHG emissions by 2050 and defining a Long-term strategic vision for a prosperous, modern, competitive and climate-neutral economy by 2050",""],[1,"67","1","EU Greenhouse Gas Emissions Reduction Target","it is planned to further reduce GHG emissions by at least 55% by 2030 compared to 1990 levels",""],[1,"67","3","Greenhouse Gas Emissions Reduction Commitment","the Republic of Serbia has voluntarily agreed to limit greenhouse gas emissions by 18% by 2020, compared to 1990 levels.",""],[1,"67","3","Nationally Determined Contribution for Emissions Reduction","In 2015, it submitted the Intended Nationally Determined Contribution (INDC) based on the UN Framework Convention on Climate Change (UNFCCC), in accordance with the Paris Climate Agreement, to reduce green- house gas emissions by 9.8% by 2030 compared to 1990.",""]],"75":[[1,"68","5","National Programme for Combating Desertification and Land Degradation","National Programme for Combating Desertification and Land Degradation, in accordance with the United Nations Convention to Combat Desertification in countries with severe drought and/or desertification",""],[1,"72","2","National Programme for Combating Desertification and Land Degradation","The strategic framework in this area will be further improved through the National Programme for Combating Desertification and Land Degradation (according to the UN Convention to Combat Desertification in Countries with Severe Drought and/or Desertification), which is under development.",""]],"76":[[1,"71","2","EU Forest Protection, Restoration and Resilience Strategy","EU Forest Strategy for 2030 provides a framework for strengthening the protection, restoration and resilience of forests at EU level.",""],[1,"72","1","Forestry Development Strategy","the Forestry Development Strategy (not time-bound and no accompanying AP) is important for achieving sustainable management of all types of forests (15.2).",""],[1,"72","1","National Forestry Programme","A key element to support the implementation of the Strategy is the National Forestry Programme, which provides an action framework for the development of the forestry sector.",""],[1,"72","1","General and Special Forest Management Planning System","The forestry planning system takes place on two levels: the level of general forest development planning, i.e. planning the purpose and function of forests within larger areas, regardless of the ownership and the level of special forest management planning at the level of management units, where the responsibility lies with the owner or user of forests.",""],[1,"73","2","Stable and Continuous Forestry Financing Policy","Forestry Development Strategy (not time-bound and no accompanying AP), within the general goal, defines the need for stable and continuous financing of activities for the improvement and protection of forests.",""],[1,"115","3","Sustainable Forest Management Financing and Promotion","Finance and encourage sustainable forest management (15.b)",""]],"77":[[1,"71","5","Spatial Planning for Environmental Protection and Land Rehabilitation","The draft Spatial Plan of the Republic of Serbia from 2021 to 2035 states that one of the goals is preventive protection and improvement of the quality of the environment, along with the rehabilitation and revitalization of endangered and degraded areas.",""],[1,"106","7","National Strategy for Sustainable Use of Natural Resources and Assets","National Strategy for Sustainable Use of Natural Resources and Assets (not time-bound and no accompanying AP)",""],[1,"110","8","National Strategy for Sustainable Use of Natural Resources and Assets","National Strategy for Sustain- able Use of Natural Resources and Assets (not time-bound and no accompanying AP)",""],[1,"113","4","National Strategy for Sustainable Use of Natural Resources and Assets","National Strategy for Sustainable Use of Natural Resources and Assets (not time-bound and no accompanying AP).",""],[1,"113","10","National Strategy for Sustainable Use of Natural Resources and Assets","National Strategy for Sustain- able Use of Natural Resources and Assets (not time-bound and no accompanying AP)",""]],"78":[[1,"75","3","Agricultural Investment Expansion","It is necessary to increase investments in: rural infrastructure, agricultural research and ex- tension services, technology development and plant and livestock gene banks (2.a).",""],[1,"75","4","IPARD Programme for Agricultural Activities Improvement","Through the IPARD programme for the Republic of Serbia for the period from 2014 to 2020, additional funds were provided for the improvement of agricultural activities.",""],[1,"76","5","Rural Development Programme","Rural development programme (under preparation) will additionally contribute towards the progress in the implementation of 2.3, 2.4 and 2.2.",""],[1,"95","7","Agriculture and Rural Development Strategy","Strategy for Agriculture and Rural Development of the Republic of Serbia for the period 2014 to 2023 (no accompanying AP) .",""],[1,"95","7","IPARD Programme for Serbia","IPARD Programme for the Republic of Serbia for the period 2014 to 2020 (modified with the Conclusion of 16 April 2021);",""],[1,"95","7","Rural Development Programme","Rural Development Programme (under preparation)",""]],"79":[[1,"76","4","National Programme for Prevention of Overweight","National Programme for Prevention of Overweight in Children and Adults (no accompanying AP) defines goals to be attained by 2025: promote healthy ways of living and improve health of the entire population and reduce overweight incidence in children, youth, adults and elderly popula- tion.",""],[1,"95","4","National Overweight Prevention Programme for Children and Adults","National Overweight Preven- tion Programme for Children and Adults (no accompanying AP)",""]],"80":[[1,"77","1","SDG 17 Partnership for the Goals","Since the funds are crucial for the implementation of the 2030 Agenda, a special SDG 17 Partner- ship for the goals was defined.",""],[1,"78","2","Continuation of Horizon 2021-2027 Scientific Cooperation","The con- tinuation of cooperation within the Horizon 2021-2027 programme is also planned.",""],[1,"78","5","Capacity Building for National Plan Implementation","it is vital to use international support for capacity building for development and implementation of national plans (17.9) in the most efficient and effective manner, including sustainable develop- ment goals.",""],[1,"79","6","Multiannual Action Plan for Regional Economic Area","since July 2017 has been a part of the Regional Economic Area and has actively participated in the development and implementation of the Multiannual Action Plan for Regional Economic Area (MAP REA), which consists of 4 dimensions: trade, investment, mobility and digital integration.",""],[1,"79","6","Common Regional Market Establishment Action Plan","The Action Plan for the establishment of a common regional market is based on four freedoms: movements - goods, services, capital and people, with improvements in the region's attractiveness for investment, integration of the Western Balkans into the pan-Eu- ropean digital space and improving the development of the industrial base and innovation infra- structure.",""],[1,"80","1","Public-Private Partnership Project Appraisal","The Public-Private Partnership Commission gave a positive opinion on 168 public-private partnership project proposals with or without concession elements.",""],[1,"80","4","EU Pre-Accession Assistance and Sectoral Cooperation","Sectoral cooperation is partly implemented using the funds available under the Pre-accession instrument IPA, and partly through bilateral financial assistance of individual countries.",""],[1,"80","4","Western Balkan Investment Framework","Western Balkan Investment Framework, WBIF, is a financial instrument and a joint initiative of the European Commission, international financial institutions, bilateral donors and six countries of the Western Balkans.",""],[1,"80","4","Connectivity Agenda under the Berlin Process","The Connectivity Agenda is promot- ed through political leadership within the Berlin Process.",""],[1,"81","3","Participation in EU Community Programmes","By signing the Framework Agreement on the general principles for the participation in Community Programmes, Serbia has acquired the right to participate in the horizontal cooperation, i.e. Community programmes.",""],[1,"81","4","Participation in EU Support and Cooperation Programmes","The implementation of the support and cooperation programmes for the period from 2021 to 2027 has continued: Customs, Horizon Europe, Fiscalis, Single Market Program (SMP), EaSI, Creative Europe n Erasmus+.",""],[1,"82","5","International Science, Technology and Innovation Cooperation","The Scientific and Technological Development Strategy of the Republic of Serbia for the period from 2021 to 2025 \"The Power of Knowledge\" with the accompanying AP for the period from 2021 to 2023 encourages association and cooperation at the international level, which contributes to achieving the target 17.6 regional and international cooperation in the field of science, technology and innovation.",""],[1,"83","5","Southeast Europe Development Strategy 2030","Southeast Europe Development Strategy until 2030 (SEE 2030) with development dimensions (pillars): Prosperity of the region (strengthening trade, tourism and transport; improving research and development and promoting renewable energy sources; reducing the risk of natural disas- ters; digitisation and public-private partnerships), Human capital in the region (better use of hu- man resources; support for the diaspora; improving education quality) and health; development of the judiciary and public services and environmental protection) and Peace and partnership in the region (strengthening institutional capacities for the implementation of the Strategy and creating mechanisms for financing measures and activities necessary for the implementation of the Strategy while respecting transparency and accountability).",""],[1,"84","1","Revised Action Plan for the EU Strategy for the Danube Region","The revised Action Plan should be a document which will provide strategic guidelines for the implementation of the EU Strategy for the Danube Region, and establish better compatibility with other programmes and funding instruments (cohesion policy programmes, other EU in- struments and funding programmes - IPA, NDICI, ENI, CEF, LIFE, Horizon Europe, etc., as well as national/regional/local funding of the Danube countries).",""],[1,"84","2","Adriatic and Ionian Regional Cooperation Strategy","EU Strategy for the Adriatic and Ionian Region consists of 4 pillars: Blue growth (fisheries and aquaculture), environmental quality (transnational terrestrial habitats and biodiversity), connect- ing the region (maritime transport, intermodal connections to the hinterland, energy networks) and sustainable tourism (sustainable and responsible tourism management).",""],[1,"112","9","Implementation of the UNFCCC Commitment","Implement the commitment undertaken under the \"United Nations Framework Convention on Climate Change\" (13.a)",""]],"81":[[1,"81","2","Statistical System Strengthening Project","SORS has improved its capacities through the project \"Strengthening the Serbian statistical sys- tem by upgrading methodologies and standards and by the appliance of good practice.\"",""],[1,"83","2","Official Statistics Programme 2021-2025","Programme of the Official Statistics for the period from 2021 to 2025 is key strategic docu- ment contributing to the availability of high-quality, timely and reliable data (17.18).",""],[1,"83","3","Sustainable Development Goals Statistics Database Enhancement","Statistics on sustainable development goals are monitored within the existing database (https://data.stat.gov.rs). Further improvement of the content and expansion of data sources in the field of sustainable development goals is planned.",""],[1,"83","6","Sustainable Development Data and Monitoring Platform","Initiatives to measure the progress in achieving the goals of sustainable development are already being implemented in the Statistical Office of the Republic of Serbia through a database and platform for a set of indicators for sustainable development.",""]],"82":[[1,"81","6","Danube River Sustainable Water Management Cooperation","The first one is Convention on Cooperation for the Protection and Sustainable Use of the Danube River, which binds Member States to strive for sustainable and equitable water management, including conservation, improvement and rational use of surface and ground waters.",""],[1,"81","6","International Commission for the Protection of the Danube River","The International Commission for the Protection of the Danube River (ICPDR), headquartered in Vienna, was established for the implementation of this Convention.",""],[1,"81","6","Tisa River Basin International Cooperation","Within the ICPDR, pursuant to the Memorandum of Under- standing signed in 2004 in Vienna, international cooperation regarding the basin of the Tisa River has been conducted.",""]],"83":[[1,"81","6","Danube River Navigability Maintenance","The Convention aims to strengthen economic relations in the region and emphasises the need to maintain the navigability of the whole Danube River.",""],[1,"88","5","Waterborne Transport Development Strategy","Continuity in the development and improvement of transport infrastructure (SDG 9) is defined through the Strategy on Development of Waterborne Transport and Programme for Public Rail Infrastructure.",""]],"84":[[1,"83","1","Public-Private Partnership Commission","In accordance with the law, the Commission for Public-Private Partnership was established to provide professional assistance in the implementation of public-private partnerships and concessions.",""]],"85":[[1,"87","8","Child Violence Prevention and Protection Strategy","New strategies have been adopted in the period from 2020 to 2021: prevention and protection of children from violence",""],[1,"87","8","Gender-Based Violence Prevention and Response Strategy","New strategies have been adopted in the period from 2020 to 2021: ... prevention and fight against gender-based violence against women and domestic violence",""],[1,"100","4","Anti-Trafficking Strategy for Women and Children","Strategy of Prevention and Suppression of Trafficking in Human Beings, Especially Women and Children and Protection of Victims for the period from 2017 to 2022",""],[1,"100","4","Gender-Based Violence Prevention and Response Strategy","Strategy for Preventing and Combating Gender-Based Violence Against Women and Domestic Violence for the period from 2021 to 2025 and the accompanying AP for the period from 2021 to 2023",""],[1,"105","4","Strategy for Prevention and Suppression of Human Trafficking and Victim Protection","Strategy of Prevention and Suppression of Trafficking in Hu- man Beings, Especially Women and Children and Protection of Victims for the period from 2017 to 2022",""],[1,"115","8","Strategy for Preventing and Combating Gender-Based Violence Against Women and Domestic Violence","Strategy for Preventing and Combating Gender-Based Violence Against Women and Domestic Violence for the pe- riod from 2021 to 2025 and the accompanying AP for the period from 2021 to 2023",""],[1,"115","8","Strategy for Prevention and Protection of Children from Violence","Strategy for Prevention and Protection of Children from Vi- olence for the period from 2020 to 2023 and the accompanying AP for the period from 2020 to 2021",""],[1,"118","4","Child Violence Prevention and Protection Strategy","Strategy for Prevention and Protection of Children from Violence for the period from 2020 to 2023 and the accompanying AP for the period from 2020 to 2021",""],[1,"118","4","Strategy to Prevent and Combat Gender-Based Violence against Women and Domestic Violence","Strategy for Preventing and Combating Gender-Based Violence against Women and Domestic Violence for the period from 2021 to 2025 and the accompanying AP for the period from 2021 to 2023",""]],"86":[[1,"87","8","Anti-Money Laundering and Counter-Terrorism Financing Strategy","New strategies have been adopted in the period from 2020 to 2021: ... combating money laundering and terrorism financing",""],[1,"87","8","Weapons of Mass Destruction Non-Proliferation Strategy","New strategies have been adopted in the period from 2020 to 2021: ... fight against proliferation of weapons of mass destruction",""],[1,"116","4","Strategy Against Money Laundering and Terrorism Financing","Strategy Against Money Laundering and Terrorism Financing for the period from 2020 to 2025 and the accompanying AP for the period from 2020 to 2022",""],[1,"116","4","Strategy for the Control of Small Arms and Light Weapons","Strategy for the Control of Small Arms and Light Weapons for the period 2019 to 2024 (AP has expired)",""],[1,"116","4","Strategy for Combating the Proliferation of Weapons of Mass Destruction","Strategy for Combating the Proliferation of Weapons of Mass Destruction for the period from 2021 to 2025 (no AP)",""],[1,"118","4","Anti-Money Laundering and Counter-Terrorism Financing Strategy","Strategy against Money Laundering and Terrorism Financing for the period from 2020 to 2025 and the accompanying AP for the period from 2020 to 2022",""]],"87":[[1,"87","9","Environment and Health Programme","Also, the adoption of the Environment and Health Programme would contribute to the harmoniza- tion of these strategically important areas.",""]],"88":[[1,"88","3","Economic Reform Programme","Economic Reform Programme, which contains key reforms that contribute to achieving economic growth, is of particular importance.",""],[1,"88","3","Development Plan of the Republic of Serbia","The adoption of the Development Plan of the Republic of Serbia would certainly contribute to the planning of long-term economic growth.",""],[1,"120","7","Economic Reform Programme","Economic Reform Programme for the period 2021-2023",""]],"89":[[1,"88","3","Strategy for Supporting the Development of Small and Medium Enterprises","In the coming period, the Strategy for Cultural Development and the Strategy for Supporting the Development of Small and Medium Enterprises should be adopted along with the setting of the institutional and legal framework for microfinance.",""],[1,"88","3","Microfinance Institutional and Legal Framework","In the coming period, the Strategy for Cultural Development and the Strategy for Supporting the Development of Small and Medium Enterprises should be adopted along with the setting of the institutional and legal framework for microfinance.",""]],"90":[[1,"88","4","Scientific and Technological Development Strategy 2021-2025","Scientific and Technological Development Strategy from 2021 to 2025 ... (adopted in 2021) greatly contribute to improving the level of innovation and research (SDG 9).",""],[1,"88","4","Smart Specialization Strategy 2020-2027","the Smart Specializa- tion Strategy from 2020 to 2027 (adopted in 2021) greatly contribute to improving the level of inno- vation and research (SDG 9).",""]],"91":[[1,"71","4","New Spatial Plan of the Republic of Serbia 2021-2035","The adoption of the new Spatial Plan of the Republic of Serbia for the period from 2021 to 2035 is expected soon (pub- lic consultations finalised).",""],[1,"88","6","Adoption of a New Spatial Plan of the Republic of Serbia","In order to preserve natural resources, it is necessary to adopt a new Spatial Plan of the Republic of Serbia and the National Environmental Protection Programme.",""],[1,"88","8","New Spatial Plan of the Republic of Serbia","it is necessary to adopt the National Housing Strategy, Road Traffic Safety Strategy, new Spatial Plan of the Republic of Serbia, Strategy for Cultural Development Strategy, Waste Management Strategy and the Air Protection Strategy.",""],[1,"113","4","Spatial Plan of the Republic of Serbia 2021-2035","Spatial Plan of the Republic of Serbia from 2021 to 2035 (public consultations finalised)",""]],"92":[[1,"88","6","Adoption of a New National Environmental Protection Programme","In order to preserve natural resources, it is necessary to adopt a new Spatial Plan of the Republic of Serbia and the National Environmental Protection Programme.",""]],"93":[[1,"88","8","National Housing Strategy","it is necessary to adopt the National Housing Strategy, Road Traffic Safety Strategy, new Spatial Plan of the Republic of Serbia, Strategy for Cultural Development Strategy, Waste Management Strategy and the Air Protection Strategy.",""],[1,"88","8","Road Traffic Safety Strategy","it is necessary to adopt the National Housing Strategy, Road Traffic Safety Strategy, new Spatial Plan of the Republic of Serbia, Strategy for Cultural Development Strategy, Waste Management Strategy and the Air Protection Strategy.",""]],"94":[[1,"82","7","Export Growth through Improved Technological Structure","One of the priorities of the Industrial Policy Strategy of the Republic of Serbia from 2021 to 2030 with the accompanying Action Plan for the period from 2021 to 2023 is to increase export (17.11).",""],[1,"104","4","Industrial Policy Strategy","Industrial Policy Strategy of the Republic of Serbia for the period from 2021 to 2030 and the accompanying AP for the period from 2021 to 2023",""],[1,"104","4","Free Zone Development Strategy","Free Zone Development Strategy of the Republic of Serbia for the period from 2018 to 2022 and the accompanying AP for the period from 2018 to 2022.",""],[1,"104","4","Doing Business Improvement Programme","Programme for Improving the Position of the Republic of Serbia on the Doing Business List of the World Bank for the period from 2020 to 2023 with the AP for the period from 2020 to 2023",""],[1,"104","7","Industrial Policy Strategy 2021-2030","Industrial Policy Strategy of the Republic of Serbia for the period from 2021 to 2030",""],[1,"104","7","Industrial Policy Action Plan 2021-2023","the accompanying AP for the period from 2021 to 2023",""],[1,"110","8","Industrial Policy Strategy","Industrial Policy Strategy of the Republic of Serbia from 2021 to 2030 and the accompanying AP for the period from 2021 to 2023",""]],"95":[[1,"104","7","Cleaner Production Programme","Cleaner Production Programme (under development)",""],[1,"110","8","Cleaner Production Programme","Cleaner Production Pro- gramme (under development);",""],[1,"111","4","Cleaner Production Programme","Cleaner Production Pro- gramme (under development).",""],[1,"111","7","Cleaner Production Programme","Cleaner Production Pro- gramme (under development).",""],[1,"112","7","Cleaner Production Programme","Cleaner Production Programme (under development)",""]],"96":[[1,"111","12","Public Procurement Development Programme","Public Procurement Develop- ment Programme in the Republic of Serbia for the period from 2019 until 2023 with its accompanying AP for 2021",""],[1,"116","6","Public Procurement Development Programme","Public Procurement Development Programme in the Repub- lic of Serbia for the period from 2019 until 2023 with its accom- panying AP for 2021",""]],"97":[[1,"115","8","Community Policing Strategy","Community Policing Strat- egy (not time-bound, AP has expired)",""],[1,"118","3","Strengthening National Institutions for Violence Prevention and Counterterrorism","Strengthen relevant national institutions for prevention of violence and combating terrorism and crime (16.a)",""]],"98":[[1,"87","8","Organized Crime Strategy Optimization Framework","Therefore, one can expect to start optimizing the planning framework in the field of public security.",""],[1,"116","4","National Strategy for the Fight Against Organised Crime","National Strategy for the Fight Against Organised Crime (not time-bound, AP has expired)",""],[1,"118","4","National Strategy for the Fight Against Organised Crime","National Strategy for the Fight Against Organised Crime (not time-bound, AP has expired)",""],[1,"118","4","Cybercrime Strategy","Strategy for the Fight Against Cybercrime for the period 2019 to 2023 (AP has expired)",""],[1,"118","4","National Counterterrorism Strategy","National Strategy for the Prevention and Fight Against the Terrorism for the period from 2016 to 2021 with the accompanying AP",""]],"99":[[1,"117","9","Aarhus Convention Implementation Strategy","Strategy for Implementing the Convention on Access to Information, Public Participation in Decision-making and Access to Justice in Environmental Matters - The Aarhus Convention (not time-bound, AP has expired)",""],[1,"117","9","Public Information System Development Strategy","Strategy for the Development of the Public Information System of the Republic of Serbia for the period from 2020 to 2025 with the accompanying AP for the period from 2020 to 2022",""],[1,"117","9","Personal Data Protection Strategy","Strategy for the Protection of Personal Data (working group has been formed)",""]]}});